{"ui_id":"u_000362_01","response_id":"r_000362_01","query_id":"q_000362","intent":"Localization","tags":["travel","itinerary","dining"],"intent_bucket":"localization","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"tokyo-itinerary-1","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"tokyo-itinerary-1","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["title","assumptions_card","itinerary_tabs","restaurants_title","restaurant_1_card","restaurant_2_card","restaurant_3_card","quick_actions_title","quick_actions_row"]},{"id":"title","component":"Text","variant":"h1","text":"Tokyo 5-Day Itinerary: Shinjuku & Shibuya Focus"},{"id":"assumptions_card","component":"Card","child":"assumptions_column"},{"id":"assumptions_column","component":"Column","children":["assumptions_title","assumption_1","assumption_2","assumption_3"]},{"id":"assumptions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Assumptions"},{"id":"assumption_1","component":"Text","text":"- The trip dates 2025-05-15 to 2025-05-20 imply 5 full days of activities (May 15th, 16th, 17th, 18th, 19th), with May 20th being a departure day. The itinerary covers these 5 activity days."},{"id":"assumption_2","component":"Text","text":"- The budget of $50 per person per meal is for a main course and perhaps a drink/side, not including very expensive extras or alcohol."},{"id":"assumption_3","component":"Text","text":"- Travel within Tokyo will primarily be via its efficient public transport system (trains/subways)."},{"id":"itinerary_tabs","component":"Tabs","tabs":[{"title":"Day 1: May 15","child":"day_1_content"},{"title":"Day 2: May 16","child":"day_2_content"},{"title":"Day 3: May 17","child":"day_3_content"},{"title":"Day 4: May 18","child":"day_4_content"},{"title":"Day 5: May 19","child":"day_5_content"}]},{"id":"day_1_content","component":"Column","children":["day_1_title","day_1_morning_title","day_1_morning_desc","day_1_afternoon_title","day_1_afternoon_desc","day_1_late_afternoon_title","day_1_late_afternoon_desc","day_1_evening_title","day_1_evening_desc"]},{"id":"day_1_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Day 1: Thursday, May 15, 2025 - Shinjuku Arrival & Gardens"},{"id":"day_1_morning_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Morning"},{"id":"day_1_morning_desc","component":"Text","text":"Arrive in Tokyo, check into your accommodation in Shinjuku or Shibuya."},{"id":"day_1_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Afternoon"},{"id":"day_1_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden - Enjoy a peaceful stroll through this beautiful imperial garden."},{"id":"day_1_late_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Late Afternoon"},{"id":"day_1_late_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building - Head to the free observation decks for panoramic views of Tokyo."},{"id":"day_1_evening_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Evening"},{"id":"day_1_evening_desc","component":"Text","text":"Dinner in Shinjuku. Explore Shinjuku Golden Gai or Omoide Yokocho (Piss Alley) for a glimpse into traditional Tokyo nightlife and small eateries (for atmosphere, not necessarily dinner)."},{"id":"day_2_content","component":"Column","children":["day_2_title","day_2_morning_title","day_2_morning_desc","day_2_afternoon_title","day_2_afternoon_desc","day_2_evening_title","day_2_evening_desc"]},{"id":"day_2_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Day 2: Friday, May 16, 2025 - Shibuya Icons & Views"},{"id":"day_2_morning_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Morning"},{"id":"day_2_morning_desc","component":"Text","text":"Shibuya Crossing & Hachiko Statue - Experience the iconic scramble crossing and meet the famous loyal dog statue."},{"id":"day_2_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Afternoon"},{"id":"day_2_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Shibuya Sky - Ascend to the rooftop observation deck for breathtaking 360-degree views of the city. Explore Shibuya Center Gai for trendy shops."},{"id":"day_2_evening_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Evening"},{"id":"day_2_evening_desc","component":"Text","text":"Dinner in Shibuya. Enjoy shopping around Shibuya 109 and other department stores."},{"id":"day_3_content","component":"Column","children":["day_3_title","day_3_morning_title","day_3_morning_desc","day_3_afternoon_title","day_3_afternoon_desc","day_3_evening_title","day_3_evening_desc"]},{"id":"day_3_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Day 3: Saturday, May 17, 2025 - Shinjuku Shopping & Culture"},{"id":"day_3_morning_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Morning"},{"id":"day_3_morning_desc","component":"Text","text":"Shinjuku Shopping Spree - Explore major department stores like Isetan, Takashimaya Times Square, and Lumine EST for a mix of high-end and trendy Japanese fashion."},{"id":"day_3_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Afternoon"},{"id":"day_3_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Samurai Museum (optional) - Immerse yourself in the history of the samurai. Alternatively, explore the quieter side streets of Shinjuku."},{"id":"day_3_evening_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Evening"},{"id":"day_3_evening_desc","component":"Text","text":"Dinner in Shinjuku. Discover the vibrant atmosphere of Kabukicho (Shinjuku's entertainment district) without necessarily engaging in its nightlife."},{"id":"day_4_content","component":"Column","children":["day_4_title","day_4_morning_title","day_4_morning_desc","day_4_afternoon_title","day_4_afternoon_desc","day_4_evening_title","day_4_evening_desc"]},{"id":"day_4_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Day 4: Sunday, May 18, 2025 - Harajuku Fashion & Meiji Jingu"},{"id":"day_4_morning_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Morning"},{"id":"day_4_morning_desc","component":"Text","text":"Meiji Jingu Shrine - Visit this serene Shinto shrine dedicated to Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken, located in a large forested area."},{"id":"day_4_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Afternoon"},{"id":"day_4_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Harajuku Exploration - Dive into Takeshita Street for quirky fashion and sweets, then stroll Omotesando for upscale boutiques and cafes. Wander down Cat Street for unique finds."},{"id":"day_4_evening_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Evening"},{"id":"day_4_evening_desc","component":"Text","text":"Dinner in Harajuku or return to Shibuya/Shinjuku. Consider a themed cafe experience if interested."},{"id":"day_5_content","component":"Column","children":["day_5_title","day_5_morning_title","day_5_morning_desc","day_5_afternoon_title","day_5_afternoon_desc","day_5_evening_title","day_5_evening_desc"]},{"id":"day_5_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Day 5: Monday, May 19, 2025 - Modern Art & Departure Prep"},{"id":"day_5_morning_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Morning"},{"id":"day_5_morning_desc","component":"Text","text":"TeamLab Planets TOKYO (Toyosu) - Experience an immersive digital art museum. (Note: This requires a short train ride from Shinjuku/Shibuya to Toyosu. Book tickets in advance.)"},{"id":"day_5_afternoon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Afternoon"},{"id":"day_5_afternoon_desc","component":"Text","text":"Last-minute Souvenir Shopping & Packing - Grab any final gifts or items you might have missed in Shinjuku or Shibuya."},{"id":"day_5_evening_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Evening"},{"id":"day_5_evening_desc","component":"Text","text":"Farewell Dinner - Enjoy a final memorable meal in one of your favorite districts."},{"id":"restaurants_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Restaurant Recommendations"},{"id":"restaurant_1_card","component":"Card","child":"restaurant_1_column"},{"id":"restaurant_1_column","component":"Column","children":["restaurant_1_name","restaurant_1_summary","restaurant_1_attr","restaurant_1_link_button"]},{"id":"restaurant_1_name","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Afuri Ramen"},{"id":"restaurant_1_summary","component":"Text","text":"Famous for its refreshing yuzu-scented broth, Afuri offers a lighter, yet flavorful ramen experience."},{"id":"restaurant_1_attr","component":"Text","text":"Key attribute: Yuzu Shio Ramen, typically under $15 per person."},{"id":"restaurant_1_link_button","component":"Button","variant":"borderless","child":"restaurant_1_link_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://afuri.com/"}}}},{"id":"restaurant_1_link_text","component":"Text","text":"EXAMPLE: https://afuri.com/"},{"id":"restaurant_2_card","component":"Card","child":"restaurant_2_column"},{"id":"restaurant_2_column","component":"Column","children":["restaurant_2_name","restaurant_2_summary","restaurant_2_attr","restaurant_2_link_button"]},{"id":"restaurant_2_name","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Katsukura Shinjuku Takashimaya"},{"id":"restaurant_2_summary","component":"Text","text":"A highly-regarded tonkatsu (fried pork cutlet) restaurant offering premium pork, which you grind your own sesame seeds for the sauce."},{"id":"restaurant_2_attr","component":"Text","text":"Key attribute: High-quality Tonkatsu sets, around $20-$30 per person."},{"id":"restaurant_2_link_button","component":"Button","variant":"borderless","child":"restaurant_2_link_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.katsukura.jp/"}}}},{"id":"restaurant_2_link_text","component":"Text","text":"EXAMPLE: https://www.katsukura.jp/"},{"id":"restaurant_3_card","component":"Card","child":"restaurant_3_column"},{"id":"restaurant_3_column","component":"Column","children":["restaurant_3_name","restaurant_3_summary","restaurant_3_attr","restaurant_3_link_button"]},{"id":"restaurant_3_name","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Uobei Sushi (Shibuya)"},{"id":"restaurant_3_summary","component":"Text","text":"A lively and modern conveyor-belt sushi restaurant where orders are placed via touch screen and delivered directly to your table on a high-speed lane."},{"id":"restaurant_3_attr","component":"Text","text":"Key attribute: Fresh, affordable sushi delivered fast, typically under $20 per person."},{"id":"restaurant_3_link_button","component":"Button","variant":"borderless","child":"restaurant_3_link_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.genkisushi.co.jp/uobei/"}}}},{"id":"restaurant_3_link_text","component":"Text","text":"EXAMPLE: https://www.genkisushi.co.jp/uobei/"},{"id":"quick_actions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Quick Actions"},{"id":"quick_actions_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceAround","children":["flights_button","hotels_button","metro_button","teamlab_button"]},{"id":"flights_button","component":"Button","child":"flights_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.google.com/flights"}}}},{"id":"flights_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Book Flights to Tokyo"},{"id":"hotels_button","component":"Button","child":"hotels_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.booking.com/city/jp/tokyo.html"}}}},{"id":"hotels_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Find Hotels in Shinjuku/Shibuya"},{"id":"metro_button","component":"Button","child":"metro_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.tokyometro.jp/en/ticket/travel/"}}}},{"id":"metro_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Explore Tokyo Metro Pass"},{"id":"teamlab_button","component":"Button","child":"teamlab_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://planets.teamlab.art/tokyo/"}}}},{"id":"teamlab_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Reserve TeamLab Tickets"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: tokyo-itinerary-1\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: tokyo-itinerary-1\n      components[83]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[9]: title,assumptions_card,itinerary_tabs,restaurants_title,restaurant_1_card,restaurant_2_card,restaurant_3_card,quick_actions_title,quick_actions_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: title\n          text: \"Tokyo 5-Day Itinerary: Shinjuku & Shibuya Focus\"\n          variant: h1\n        - child: assumptions_column\n          component: Card\n          id: assumptions_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: assumptions_column\n          children[4]: assumptions_title,assumption_1,assumption_2,assumption_3\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_title\n          text: Assumptions\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumption_1\n          text: \"- The trip dates 2025-05-15 to 2025-05-20 imply 5 full days of activities (May 15th, 16th, 17th, 18th, 19th), with May 20th being a departure day. The itinerary covers these 5 activity days.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumption_2\n          text: \"- The budget of $50 per person per meal is for a main course and perhaps a drink/side, not including very expensive extras or alcohol.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumption_3\n          text: \"- Travel within Tokyo will primarily be via its efficient public transport system (trains/subways).\"\n        - component: Tabs\n          id: itinerary_tabs\n          tabs[5]{child,title}:\n            day_1_content,\"Day 1: May 15\"\n            day_2_content,\"Day 2: May 16\"\n            day_3_content,\"Day 3: May 17\"\n            day_4_content,\"Day 4: May 18\"\n            day_5_content,\"Day 5: May 19\"\n        - component: Column\n          id: day_1_content\n          children[9]: day_1_title,day_1_morning_title,day_1_morning_desc,day_1_afternoon_title,day_1_afternoon_desc,day_1_late_afternoon_title,day_1_late_afternoon_desc,day_1_evening_title,day_1_evening_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_title\n          text: \"Day 1: Thursday, May 15, 2025 - Shinjuku Arrival & Gardens\"\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_morning_title\n          text: Morning\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_morning_desc\n          text: \"Arrive in Tokyo, check into your accommodation in Shinjuku or Shibuya.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_afternoon_title\n          text: Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_afternoon_desc\n          text: Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden - Enjoy a peaceful stroll through this beautiful imperial garden.\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_late_afternoon_title\n          text: Late Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_late_afternoon_desc\n          text: Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building - Head to the free observation decks for panoramic views of Tokyo.\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_evening_title\n          text: Evening\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_1_evening_desc\n          text: \"Dinner in Shinjuku. Explore Shinjuku Golden Gai or Omoide Yokocho (Piss Alley) for a glimpse into traditional Tokyo nightlife and small eateries (for atmosphere, not necessarily dinner).\"\n        - component: Column\n          id: day_2_content\n          children[7]: day_2_title,day_2_morning_title,day_2_morning_desc,day_2_afternoon_title,day_2_afternoon_desc,day_2_evening_title,day_2_evening_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_title\n          text: \"Day 2: Friday, May 16, 2025 - Shibuya Icons & Views\"\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_morning_title\n          text: Morning\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_morning_desc\n          text: Shibuya Crossing & Hachiko Statue - Experience the iconic scramble crossing and meet the famous loyal dog statue.\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_afternoon_title\n          text: Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_afternoon_desc\n          text: Shibuya Sky - Ascend to the rooftop observation deck for breathtaking 360-degree views of the city. Explore Shibuya Center Gai for trendy shops.\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_evening_title\n          text: Evening\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_2_evening_desc\n          text: Dinner in Shibuya. Enjoy shopping around Shibuya 109 and other department stores.\n        - component: Column\n          id: day_3_content\n          children[7]: day_3_title,day_3_morning_title,day_3_morning_desc,day_3_afternoon_title,day_3_afternoon_desc,day_3_evening_title,day_3_evening_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_title\n          text: \"Day 3: Saturday, May 17, 2025 - Shinjuku Shopping & Culture\"\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_morning_title\n          text: Morning\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_morning_desc\n          text: \"Shinjuku Shopping Spree - Explore major department stores like Isetan, Takashimaya Times Square, and Lumine EST for a mix of high-end and trendy Japanese fashion.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_afternoon_title\n          text: Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_afternoon_desc\n          text: \"Samurai Museum (optional) - Immerse yourself in the history of the samurai. Alternatively, explore the quieter side streets of Shinjuku.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_evening_title\n          text: Evening\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_3_evening_desc\n          text: Dinner in Shinjuku. Discover the vibrant atmosphere of Kabukicho (Shinjuku's entertainment district) without necessarily engaging in its nightlife.\n        - component: Column\n          id: day_4_content\n          children[7]: day_4_title,day_4_morning_title,day_4_morning_desc,day_4_afternoon_title,day_4_afternoon_desc,day_4_evening_title,day_4_evening_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_title\n          text: \"Day 4: Sunday, May 18, 2025 - Harajuku Fashion & Meiji Jingu\"\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_morning_title\n          text: Morning\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_morning_desc\n          text: \"Meiji Jingu Shrine - Visit this serene Shinto shrine dedicated to Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken, located in a large forested area.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_afternoon_title\n          text: Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_afternoon_desc\n          text: \"Harajuku Exploration - Dive into Takeshita Street for quirky fashion and sweets, then stroll Omotesando for upscale boutiques and cafes. Wander down Cat Street for unique finds.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_evening_title\n          text: Evening\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_4_evening_desc\n          text: Dinner in Harajuku or return to Shibuya/Shinjuku. Consider a themed cafe experience if interested.\n        - component: Column\n          id: day_5_content\n          children[7]: day_5_title,day_5_morning_title,day_5_morning_desc,day_5_afternoon_title,day_5_afternoon_desc,day_5_evening_title,day_5_evening_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_title\n          text: \"Day 5: Monday, May 19, 2025 - Modern Art & Departure Prep\"\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_morning_title\n          text: Morning\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_morning_desc\n          text: \"TeamLab Planets TOKYO (Toyosu) - Experience an immersive digital art museum. (Note: This requires a short train ride from Shinjuku/Shibuya to Toyosu. Book tickets in advance.)\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_afternoon_title\n          text: Afternoon\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_afternoon_desc\n          text: Last-minute Souvenir Shopping & Packing - Grab any final gifts or items you might have missed in Shinjuku or Shibuya.\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_evening_title\n          text: Evening\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: day_5_evening_desc\n          text: Farewell Dinner - Enjoy a final memorable meal in one of your favorite districts.\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurants_title\n          text: Restaurant Recommendations\n          variant: h2\n        - child: restaurant_1_column\n          component: Card\n          id: restaurant_1_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: restaurant_1_column\n          children[4]: restaurant_1_name,restaurant_1_summary,restaurant_1_attr,restaurant_1_link_button\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_1_name\n          text: Afuri Ramen\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_1_summary\n          text: \"Famous for its refreshing yuzu-scented broth, Afuri offers a lighter, yet flavorful ramen experience.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_1_attr\n          text: \"Key attribute: Yuzu Shio Ramen, typically under $15 per person.\"\n        - child: restaurant_1_link_text\n          component: Button\n          id: restaurant_1_link_button\n          variant: borderless\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://afuri.com/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_1_link_text\n          text: \"EXAMPLE: https://afuri.com/\"\n        - child: restaurant_2_column\n          component: Card\n          id: restaurant_2_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: restaurant_2_column\n          children[4]: restaurant_2_name,restaurant_2_summary,restaurant_2_attr,restaurant_2_link_button\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_2_name\n          text: Katsukura Shinjuku Takashimaya\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_2_summary\n          text: \"A highly-regarded tonkatsu (fried pork cutlet) restaurant offering premium pork, which you grind your own sesame seeds for the sauce.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_2_attr\n          text: \"Key attribute: High-quality Tonkatsu sets, around $20-$30 per person.\"\n        - child: restaurant_2_link_text\n          component: Button\n          id: restaurant_2_link_button\n          variant: borderless\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.katsukura.jp/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_2_link_text\n          text: \"EXAMPLE: https://www.katsukura.jp/\"\n        - child: restaurant_3_column\n          component: Card\n          id: restaurant_3_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: restaurant_3_column\n          children[4]: restaurant_3_name,restaurant_3_summary,restaurant_3_attr,restaurant_3_link_button\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_3_name\n          text: Uobei Sushi (Shibuya)\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_3_summary\n          text: A lively and modern conveyor-belt sushi restaurant where orders are placed via touch screen and delivered directly to your table on a high-speed lane.\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_3_attr\n          text: \"Key attribute: Fresh, affordable sushi delivered fast, typically under $20 per person.\"\n        - child: restaurant_3_link_text\n          component: Button\n          id: restaurant_3_link_button\n          variant: borderless\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.genkisushi.co.jp/uobei/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: restaurant_3_link_text\n          text: \"EXAMPLE: https://www.genkisushi.co.jp/uobei/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: quick_actions_title\n          text: Quick Actions\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Row\n          id: quick_actions_row\n          justify: spaceAround\n          children[4]: flights_button,hotels_button,metro_button,teamlab_button\n        - child: flights_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: flights_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.google.com/flights\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: flights_button_text\n          text: Book Flights to Tokyo\n        - child: hotels_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: hotels_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.booking.com/city/jp/tokyo.html\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: hotels_button_text\n          text: Find Hotels in Shinjuku/Shibuya\n        - child: metro_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: metro_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.tokyometro.jp/en/ticket/travel/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: metro_button_text\n          text: Explore Tokyo Metro Pass\n        - child: teamlab_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: teamlab_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://planets.teamlab.art/tokyo/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: teamlab_button_text\n          text: Reserve TeamLab Tickets","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9452449567723343,"dup_rate":0.3096446700507614,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":1252,"output_tokens_json":1236,"component_count":83.0,"unique_component_types":6.0,"max_tree_depth":5.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.4337349397590362,"container_to_text_ratio":0.26666666666666666,"information_chunking_score":0.9503008108815066,"ui_modularity_score":0.060240963855421686,"ui_decomposition_score":0.417342625362379,"actionable_elements":7.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.42857142857142855,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.6666666666666666,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.05,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":1.0,"intent_expectation_pass":1.0,"intent_score":1.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":48901.97658538818,"input_tokens":15200,"output_tokens":5427,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:22:25.124271Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000401_01","response_id":"r_000401_01","query_id":"q_000401","intent":"Technical support","tags":["software troubleshooting","excel","data formatting"],"intent_bucket":"technical_support","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"vlookup-error-fix-surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"vlookup-error-fix-surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["summary_title","summary_text","assumptions_title","assumptions_text","solution1_title","solution1_desc","solution1_exp_title","solution1_exp_text","solution1_steps_title","solution1_steps_text","solution1_example_title","solution1_example_desc","solution1_example1_card","solution1_example2_card","solution2_title","solution2_desc","solution2_exp_title","solution2_exp_text","solution2_steps_title","solution2_steps_text","solution2_alt_title","solution2_alt_text","comparison_title","comparison_table","actions_title","actions_row"]},{"id":"summary_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Summary"},{"id":"summary_text","component":"Text","text":"A common VLOOKUP error occurs when the lookup value and the first column of the source table have different data types (e.g., one is text, the other is a number), even if they appear identical. This response provides two methods to resolve this: a formula-based solution that converts the lookup value, and a formatting-based solution that converts the source data."},{"id":"assumptions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Assumptions"},{"id":"assumptions_text","component":"Text","text":"*   The lookup value is in a cell (e.g., A2) and is currently formatted as text.\n*   The first column of your source table (where VLOOKUP searches) contains numbers, but the lookup value is not matching due to its text format.\n*   The VLOOKUP formula is otherwise correctly structured."},{"id":"solution1_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Solution 1: Formula-Based Approach (Convert Lookup Value to Number)"},{"id":"solution1_desc","component":"Text","text":"This method modifies your VLOOKUP formula to convert the text lookup value into a number *before* performing the lookup, without altering your original data."},{"id":"solution1_exp_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Explanation"},{"id":"solution1_exp_text","component":"Text","text":"Excel's VLOOKUP requires the data types to match for an exact match. By converting the text lookup value to a number within the formula, you ensure compatibility with the numeric data in your source table."},{"id":"solution1_steps_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Steps"},{"id":"solution1_steps_text","component":"Text","text":"1.  Identify the cell containing your text-formatted lookup value (e.g., A2).\n2.  Modify your VLOOKUP formula to convert this text value to a number using a suitable function or operator."},{"id":"solution1_example_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Example Formula"},{"id":"solution1_example_desc","component":"Text","text":"If your original formula was `=VLOOKUP(A2, B:C, 2, FALSE)` and cell A2 contains a text value like \"123\", you can use one of these modified formulas:"},{"id":"solution1_example1_card","component":"Card","child":"solution1_example1_text"},{"id":"solution1_example1_text","component":"Text","text":"**Using Double Unary Operator:**\n`=VLOOKUP(--A2, B:C, 2, FALSE)`\n(The double unary operator (--) is a concise way to convert text representations of numbers into actual numbers.)"},{"id":"solution1_example2_card","component":"Card","child":"solution1_example2_text"},{"id":"solution1_example2_text","component":"Text","text":"**Using VALUE Function:**\n`=VLOOKUP(VALUE(A2), B:C, 2, FALSE)`"},{"id":"solution2_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Solution 2: Formatting-Based Approach (Convert Source Data to Number)"},{"id":"solution2_desc","component":"Text","text":"This method involves permanently changing the data type of the relevant column in your source table from text to number."},{"id":"solution2_exp_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Explanation"},{"id":"solution2_exp_text","component":"Text","text":"If the numbers in your source table's lookup column are stored as text (often indicated by a green triangle in the top-left corner of the cell), VLOOKUP will not find a match for a numeric lookup value. Converting these to actual numbers resolves the mismatch directly in your data."},{"id":"solution2_steps_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Steps"},{"id":"solution2_steps_text","component":"Text","text":"1.  Select the entire column or range in your source table that contains the numbers currently stored as text (e.g., column B).\n2.  Look for the \"Error Checking\" smart tag (a small yellow icon with an exclamation mark) that appears when you hover over the selection or click a cell with a green triangle.\n3.  Click the dropdown arrow next to the smart tag and select \"Convert to Number\"."},{"id":"solution2_alt_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Alternative Methods to Convert Text to Number in Source Data"},{"id":"solution2_alt_text","component":"Text","text":"*   **Text to Columns:** Select the column, go to the \"Data\" tab on the Excel ribbon, click \"Text to Columns\", then simply click \"Finish\". This often forces the conversion to numbers.\n*   **Paste Special (Multiply by 1):**\n    1.  Enter the number 1 into an empty cell and copy it.\n    2.  Select the range of cells in your source table that contains the text-formatted numbers.\n    3.  Right-click on the selected range, choose \"Paste Special\", then select \"Multiply\" under \"Operation\", and click \"OK\".\n*   **Add 0:** Similar to \"Multiply by 1\", but copy a 0, then use \"Paste Special\" and \"Add\"."},{"id":"comparison_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Comparison of Solutions"},{"id":"comparison_table","component":"Text","text":"| Solution Type    | Pros                                    | Cons                                       | Best Use Case                                  |\n|------------------|-----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| Formula-Based    | Non-destructive to original source data | Requires modifying each VLOOKUP formula    | When source data cannot or should not be changed |\n| Formatting-Based | Permanent fix for source data           | Modifies original data in the worksheet    | When source data needs to be clean numeric and is safe to alter |"},{"id":"actions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Quick Actions"},{"id":"actions_row","component":"Row","justify":"start","children":["button1","button2"]},{"id":"button1","component":"Button","child":"button1_label","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/vlookup-function-0398606e-09a8-4229-9e63-c7e6c40a5a67"}}}},{"id":"button1_label","component":"Text","text":"Excel VLOOKUP Function Help"},{"id":"button2","component":"Button","child":"button2_label","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/convert-numbers-stored-as-text-to-numbers-40a1b802-5509-480f-a0c0-6296b63a9404"}}}},{"id":"button2_label","component":"Text","text":"Convert Numbers Stored as Text to Numbers"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: vlookup-error-fix-surface\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: vlookup-error-fix-surface\n      components[33]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[26]: summary_title,summary_text,assumptions_title,assumptions_text,solution1_title,solution1_desc,solution1_exp_title,solution1_exp_text,solution1_steps_title,solution1_steps_text,solution1_example_title,solution1_example_desc,solution1_example1_card,solution1_example2_card,solution2_title,solution2_desc,solution2_exp_title,solution2_exp_text,solution2_steps_title,solution2_steps_text,solution2_alt_title,solution2_alt_text,comparison_title,comparison_table,actions_title,actions_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_title\n          text: Summary\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_text\n          text: \"A common VLOOKUP error occurs when the lookup value and the first column of the source table have different data types (e.g., one is text, the other is a number), even if they appear identical. This response provides two methods to resolve this: a formula-based solution that converts the lookup value, and a formatting-based solution that converts the source data.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_title\n          text: Assumptions\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_text\n          text: \"*   The lookup value is in a cell (e.g., A2) and is currently formatted as text.\\n*   The first column of your source table (where VLOOKUP searches) contains numbers, but the lookup value is not matching due to its text format.\\n*   The VLOOKUP formula is otherwise correctly structured.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_title\n          text: \"Solution 1: Formula-Based Approach (Convert Lookup Value to Number)\"\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_desc\n          text: \"This method modifies your VLOOKUP formula to convert the text lookup value into a number *before* performing the lookup, without altering your original data.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_exp_title\n          text: Explanation\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_exp_text\n          text: \"Excel's VLOOKUP requires the data types to match for an exact match. By converting the text lookup value to a number within the formula, you ensure compatibility with the numeric data in your source table.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_steps_title\n          text: Steps\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_steps_text\n          text: \"1.  Identify the cell containing your text-formatted lookup value (e.g., A2).\\n2.  Modify your VLOOKUP formula to convert this text value to a number using a suitable function or operator.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_example_title\n          text: Example Formula\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_example_desc\n          text: \"If your original formula was `=VLOOKUP(A2, B:C, 2, FALSE)` and cell A2 contains a text value like \\\"123\\\", you can use one of these modified formulas:\"\n        - child: solution1_example1_text\n          component: Card\n          id: solution1_example1_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_example1_text\n          text: \"**Using Double Unary Operator:**\\n`=VLOOKUP(--A2, B:C, 2, FALSE)`\\n(The double unary operator (--) is a concise way to convert text representations of numbers into actual numbers.)\"\n        - child: solution1_example2_text\n          component: Card\n          id: solution1_example2_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution1_example2_text\n          text: \"**Using VALUE Function:**\\n`=VLOOKUP(VALUE(A2), B:C, 2, FALSE)`\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_title\n          text: \"Solution 2: Formatting-Based Approach (Convert Source Data to Number)\"\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_desc\n          text: This method involves permanently changing the data type of the relevant column in your source table from text to number.\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_exp_title\n          text: Explanation\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_exp_text\n          text: \"If the numbers in your source table's lookup column are stored as text (often indicated by a green triangle in the top-left corner of the cell), VLOOKUP will not find a match for a numeric lookup value. Converting these to actual numbers resolves the mismatch directly in your data.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_steps_title\n          text: Steps\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_steps_text\n          text: \"1.  Select the entire column or range in your source table that contains the numbers currently stored as text (e.g., column B).\\n2.  Look for the \\\"Error Checking\\\" smart tag (a small yellow icon with an exclamation mark) that appears when you hover over the selection or click a cell with a green triangle.\\n3.  Click the dropdown arrow next to the smart tag and select \\\"Convert to Number\\\".\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_alt_title\n          text: Alternative Methods to Convert Text to Number in Source Data\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: solution2_alt_text\n          text: \"*   **Text to Columns:** Select the column, go to the \\\"Data\\\" tab on the Excel ribbon, click \\\"Text to Columns\\\", then simply click \\\"Finish\\\". This often forces the conversion to numbers.\\n*   **Paste Special (Multiply by 1):**\\n    1.  Enter the number 1 into an empty cell and copy it.\\n    2.  Select the range of cells in your source table that contains the text-formatted numbers.\\n    3.  Right-click on the selected range, choose \\\"Paste Special\\\", then select \\\"Multiply\\\" under \\\"Operation\\\", and click \\\"OK\\\".\\n*   **Add 0:** Similar to \\\"Multiply by 1\\\", but copy a 0, then use \\\"Paste Special\\\" and \\\"Add\\\".\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: comparison_title\n          text: Comparison of Solutions\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: comparison_table\n          text: \"| Solution Type    | Pros                                    | Cons                                       | Best Use Case                                  |\\n|------------------|-----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|\\n| Formula-Based    | Non-destructive to original source data | Requires modifying each VLOOKUP formula    | When source data cannot or should not be changed |\\n| Formatting-Based | Permanent fix for source data           | Modifies original data in the worksheet    | When source data needs to be clean numeric and is safe to alter |\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: actions_title\n          text: Quick Actions\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Row\n          id: actions_row\n          justify: start\n          children[2]: button1,button2\n        - child: button1_label\n          component: Button\n          id: button1\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/vlookup-function-0398606e-09a8-4229-9e63-c7e6c40a5a67\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: button1_label\n          text: Excel VLOOKUP Function Help\n        - child: button2_label\n          component: Button\n          id: button2\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/convert-numbers-stored-as-text-to-numbers-40a1b802-5509-480f-a0c0-6296b63a9404\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: button2_label\n          text: Convert Numbers Stored as Text to Numbers","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.26136363636363635,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":861,"output_tokens_json":851,"component_count":33.0,"unique_component_types":5.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.2727272727272727,"container_to_text_ratio":0.14814814814814814,"information_chunking_score":0.8378106954556866,"ui_modularity_score":0.09090909090909091,"ui_decomposition_score":0.34985731305297796,"actionable_elements":2.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.7777777777777778,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.23255813953488372,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":1.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.6666666666666666},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":40654.173135757446,"input_tokens":15042,"output_tokens":2678,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:23:06.877469Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000402_01","response_id":"r_000402_01","query_id":"q_000402","intent":"Technical support","tags":["networking","hardware setup","router"],"intent_bucket":"technical_support","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"linksys-router-guide","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"linksys-router-guide","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["title","assumptions_title","assumption_1","assumption_2","divider_1","defaults_title","default_1","default_2","default_3","divider_2","steps_title","step_1_title","step_1_item_1","step_1_item_2","step_2_title","step_2_item_1","step_2_item_2","step_2_item_3","step_3_title","step_3_item_1","step_3_item_2","step_4_title","step_4_item_1","step_4_item_2","step_4_item_3","step_5_title","step_5_item_1","step_5_item_2","step_5_item_3","step_5_item_4","step_6_title","step_6_item_1","step_7_title","step_7_item_1","step_7_item_2","step_7_item_3","step_7_item_4","divider_3","note_card","divider_4","actions_title","support_button","divider_5","sources_title","source_1"]},{"id":"title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"How to Change SSID and Password on a Linksys EA8300 Router"},{"id":"assumptions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Assumptions"},{"id":"assumption_1","component":"Text","text":"• You are currently connected to your Linksys EA8300 router, either via Wi-Fi or an Ethernet cable."},{"id":"assumption_2","component":"Text","text":"• You know the current administrative password for your router. If you have never changed it, try the default passwords mentioned below. If you don't know it and the defaults don't work, you may need to perform a factory reset (which is beyond the scope of this guide and would erase all your custom settings)."},{"id":"divider_1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"defaults_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Default Router Access Information"},{"id":"default_1","component":"Text","text":"• Local IP Address: 192.168.1.1"},{"id":"default_2","component":"Text","text":"• Standard Administrative Username: admin"},{"id":"default_3","component":"Text","text":"• Standard Administrative Password: admin or password (or sometimes it's blank). Always check the label on the bottom or back of your physical router for the most accurate default login details."},{"id":"divider_2","component":"Divider"},{"id":"steps_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Step-by-Step Guide to Change SSID and WPA2 Password"},{"id":"step_1_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"1. Access Your Router's Web Interface"},{"id":"step_1_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• Open a web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari, etc.) on a device connected to your Linksys EA8300 router."},{"id":"step_1_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• In the address bar, type the default local IP address: 192.168.1.1 and press Enter."},{"id":"step_2_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"2. Log In to Your Router"},{"id":"step_2_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• A login screen will appear."},{"id":"step_2_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• Enter the Username (typically \"admin\") and the Password (your current router administrative password)."},{"id":"step_2_item_3","component":"Text","text":"• Click \"Log In\" or \"Sign In\"."},{"id":"step_3_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"3. Navigate to Wireless Settings"},{"id":"step_3_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• Once logged in, you will usually see a dashboard or main menu."},{"id":"step_3_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• Look for sections like \"Wi-Fi Settings\", \"Wireless\", \"Connectivity\", or \"Network\". For Linksys, it's often under \"Wi-Fi\" or \"Wireless\"."},{"id":"step_4_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"4. Change the Wi-Fi Network Name (SSID)"},{"id":"step_4_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• Within the Wireless settings, you will likely see separate sections for your 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands. You can change them individually or simultaneously if your router offers a \"Smart Connect\" or \"Band Steering\" feature that merges them into one SSID."},{"id":"step_4_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• Locate the \"Network Name (SSID)\" field for both 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands."},{"id":"step_4_item_3","component":"Text","text":"• Delete the existing name and type in your desired new Wi-Fi network name. Choose a name that is easy for you to recognize."},{"id":"step_5_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"5. Change the Wi-Fi Password (WPA2 Security Key)"},{"id":"step_5_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• In the same Wireless settings section, find the \"Security Mode\" or \"Security Type\" option. Ensure it is set to \"WPA2 Personal\" or \"WPA2/WPA3 Personal\" for the best security."},{"id":"step_5_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• Locate the \"Password\", \"Network Key\", or \"Passphrase\" field."},{"id":"step_5_item_3","component":"Text","text":"• Delete the existing password and type in your new desired Wi-Fi password."},{"id":"step_5_item_4","component":"Text","text":"• Choose a strong password that is at least 8 characters long, combining uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols."},{"id":"step_6_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"6. Save Your Changes"},{"id":"step_6_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• After making your changes to both the SSID and password, look for a \"Apply\", \"Save\", or \"OK\" button, usually at the bottom of the page. Click it to save your new settings."},{"id":"step_7_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"7. Reconnect Your Devices"},{"id":"step_7_item_1","component":"Text","text":"• Your router will likely restart or refresh its wireless network."},{"id":"step_7_item_2","component":"Text","text":"• All devices previously connected to your Wi-Fi will be disconnected."},{"id":"step_7_item_3","component":"Text","text":"• On each device (phone, laptop, tablet, smart home devices), you will need to forget the old Wi-Fi network and then search for your new Wi-Fi network name (SSID)."},{"id":"step_7_item_4","component":"Text","text":"• Select your new SSID and enter the new Wi-Fi password you just created to reconnect."},{"id":"divider_3","component":"Divider"},{"id":"note_card","component":"Card","child":"note_column"},{"id":"note_column","component":"Column","children":["note_title","note_text"]},{"id":"note_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Important Note"},{"id":"note_text","component":"Text","text":"Always remember your new SSID and Wi-Fi password. It's a good idea to write them down and keep them in a secure place."},{"id":"divider_4","component":"Divider"},{"id":"actions_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Quick Actions"},{"id":"support_button","component":"Button","child":"support_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.linksys.com/us/support/products/routers/EA8300.html"}}}},{"id":"support_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Linksys EA8300 Support Page"},{"id":"divider_5","component":"Divider"},{"id":"sources_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Sources"},{"id":"source_1","component":"Text","text":"• Linksys EA8300 Support Page: https://www.linksys.com/us/support/products/routers/EA8300.html"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: linksys-router-guide\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: linksys-router-guide\n      components[50]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[45]: title,assumptions_title,assumption_1,assumption_2,divider_1,defaults_title,default_1,default_2,default_3,divider_2,steps_title,step_1_title,step_1_item_1,step_1_item_2,step_2_title,step_2_item_1,step_2_item_2,step_2_item_3,step_3_title,step_3_item_1,step_3_item_2,step_4_title,step_4_item_1,step_4_item_2,step_4_item_3,step_5_title,step_5_item_1,step_5_item_2,step_5_item_3,step_5_item_4,step_6_title,step_6_item_1,step_7_title,step_7_item_1,step_7_item_2,step_7_item_3,step_7_item_4,divider_3,note_card,divider_4,actions_title,support_button,divider_5,sources_title,source_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: title\n          text: How to Change SSID and Password on a Linksys EA8300 Router\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_title\n          text: Assumptions\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumption_1\n          text: \"• You are currently connected to your Linksys EA8300 router, either via Wi-Fi or an Ethernet cable.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumption_2\n          text: \"• You know the current administrative password for your router. If you have never changed it, try the default passwords mentioned below. If you don't know it and the defaults don't work, you may need to perform a factory reset (which is beyond the scope of this guide and would erase all your custom settings).\"\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: defaults_title\n          text: Default Router Access Information\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: default_1\n          text: \"• Local IP Address: 192.168.1.1\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: default_2\n          text: \"• Standard Administrative Username: admin\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: default_3\n          text: \"• Standard Administrative Password: admin or password (or sometimes it's blank). Always check the label on the bottom or back of your physical router for the most accurate default login details.\"\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_2\n        - component: Text\n          id: steps_title\n          text: Step-by-Step Guide to Change SSID and WPA2 Password\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_1_title\n          text: 1. Access Your Router's Web Interface\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_1_item_1\n          text: \"• Open a web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari, etc.) on a device connected to your Linksys EA8300 router.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_1_item_2\n          text: \"• In the address bar, type the default local IP address: 192.168.1.1 and press Enter.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_2_title\n          text: 2. Log In to Your Router\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_2_item_1\n          text: • A login screen will appear.\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_2_item_2\n          text: \"• Enter the Username (typically \\\"admin\\\") and the Password (your current router administrative password).\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_2_item_3\n          text: \"• Click \\\"Log In\\\" or \\\"Sign In\\\".\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_3_title\n          text: 3. Navigate to Wireless Settings\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_3_item_1\n          text: \"• Once logged in, you will usually see a dashboard or main menu.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_3_item_2\n          text: \"• Look for sections like \\\"Wi-Fi Settings\\\", \\\"Wireless\\\", \\\"Connectivity\\\", or \\\"Network\\\". For Linksys, it's often under \\\"Wi-Fi\\\" or \\\"Wireless\\\".\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_4_title\n          text: 4. Change the Wi-Fi Network Name (SSID)\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_4_item_1\n          text: \"• Within the Wireless settings, you will likely see separate sections for your 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands. You can change them individually or simultaneously if your router offers a \\\"Smart Connect\\\" or \\\"Band Steering\\\" feature that merges them into one SSID.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_4_item_2\n          text: \"• Locate the \\\"Network Name (SSID)\\\" field for both 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_4_item_3\n          text: • Delete the existing name and type in your desired new Wi-Fi network name. Choose a name that is easy for you to recognize.\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_5_title\n          text: 5. Change the Wi-Fi Password (WPA2 Security Key)\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_5_item_1\n          text: \"• In the same Wireless settings section, find the \\\"Security Mode\\\" or \\\"Security Type\\\" option. Ensure it is set to \\\"WPA2 Personal\\\" or \\\"WPA2/WPA3 Personal\\\" for the best security.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_5_item_2\n          text: \"• Locate the \\\"Password\\\", \\\"Network Key\\\", or \\\"Passphrase\\\" field.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_5_item_3\n          text: • Delete the existing password and type in your new desired Wi-Fi password.\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_5_item_4\n          text: \"• Choose a strong password that is at least 8 characters long, combining uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_6_title\n          text: 6. Save Your Changes\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_6_item_1\n          text: \"• After making your changes to both the SSID and password, look for a \\\"Apply\\\", \\\"Save\\\", or \\\"OK\\\" button, usually at the bottom of the page. Click it to save your new settings.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_7_title\n          text: 7. Reconnect Your Devices\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_7_item_1\n          text: • Your router will likely restart or refresh its wireless network.\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_7_item_2\n          text: • All devices previously connected to your Wi-Fi will be disconnected.\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_7_item_3\n          text: \"• On each device (phone, laptop, tablet, smart home devices), you will need to forget the old Wi-Fi network and then search for your new Wi-Fi network name (SSID).\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: step_7_item_4\n          text: • Select your new SSID and enter the new Wi-Fi password you just created to reconnect.\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_3\n        - child: note_column\n          component: Card\n          id: note_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: note_column\n          children[2]: note_title,note_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: note_title\n          text: Important Note\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: note_text\n          text: Always remember your new SSID and Wi-Fi password. It's a good idea to write them down and keep them in a secure place.\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_4\n        - component: Text\n          id: actions_title\n          text: Quick Actions\n          variant: h3\n        - child: support_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: support_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.linksys.com/us/support/products/routers/EA8300.html\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: support_button_text\n          text: Linksys EA8300 Support Page\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_5\n        - component: Text\n          id: sources_title\n          text: Sources\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: source_1\n          text: \"• Linksys EA8300 Support Page: https://www.linksys.com/us/support/products/routers/EA8300.html\"","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":["json_parse_error: Expecting ',' delimiter: line 274 column 12 (char 9278)"],"repair_attempts":1,"repair_needed":true},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.2384937238493724,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":911,"output_tokens_json":903,"component_count":50.0,"unique_component_types":5.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.14,"container_to_text_ratio":0.07317073170731707,"information_chunking_score":0.9070185962807439,"ui_modularity_score":0.02,"ui_decomposition_score":0.32847688998785607,"actionable_elements":1.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.5,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.375,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.5},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":118919.61979866028,"input_tokens":14897,"output_tokens":3098,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:26:01.471050Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000441_01","response_id":"r_000441_01","query_id":"q_000441","intent":"Creating Writing","tags":["creative writing","historical fiction","short story"],"intent_bucket":"creative_writing","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"clockmaker_story_surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"clockmaker_story_surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["title","story_image","story_card"]},{"id":"title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"The Clockmaker's Five Seconds"},{"id":"story_image","component":"Image","url":"/images/prague_clock_shop_1895.png","variant":"header","accessibility":{"label":"An old clock shop in Prague in 1895, filled with intricate clocks and gears."}},{"id":"story_card","component":"Card","child":"card_content"},{"id":"card_content","component":"Column","children":["p1","p2","p3","p4","p5"]},{"id":"p1","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Josef Kovář, a man whose hands moved with the precision of the gears he meticulously crafted, owned a small, unassuming clock shop nestled in the labyrinthine alleys of Prague in the year 1895. His shop, \"Časové Kouzlo\" (Time's Magic), was a sanctuary of ticking, chiming, and the gentle whir of unseen mechanisms. Josef, a bachelor in his late forties, lived for the intricate dance of springs and cogs."},{"id":"p2","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"One crisp autumn evening, while disassembling an antique pocket watch brought in by a reclusive count, Josef discovered a peculiar additional mechanism. It was a tiny, almost invisible lever, connected to a crystal that pulsed with a faint, otherworldly blue light when activated. Driven by an insatiable curiosity, Josef spent weeks studying it, sacrificing sleep and meals. Finally, with a trembling hand, he pressed the lever."},{"id":"p3","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"The world around him froze. The pendulum of the grandfather clock in the corner hung mid-swing, a dust motes suspended in the air like tiny, frozen stars, and the distant clatter of a horse-drawn carriage from outside vanished into an absolute silence. Josef, however, could move freely. He checked his own pocket watch – exactly five seconds had passed when the world snapped back into motion, the pendulum resuming its swing with a soft 'tick-tock', the dust motes falling, and the carriage sound returning. He had stumbled upon a device that could halt time itself, for precisely five seconds. He named it the \"Chronos Shard.\""},{"id":"p4","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"A week later, the Chronos Shard found its purpose. Josef was perched precariously on a tall stool, reaching for a rare, gilded cuckoo clock on a high shelf. Below him, his young apprentice, Karel, was meticulously polishing a display case filled with delicate porcelain figurines. As Josef stretched, his elbow accidentally nudged a stack of finely crafted wooden gears he had left on the edge of his workbench. They teetered, threatening to cascade down onto Karel and the fragile porcelain below. A scream caught in Karel's throat as he looked up, eyes wide with horror."},{"id":"p5","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Without a moment's hesitation, Josef's hand flew to his waistcoat pocket, retrieving the Chronos Shard. He pressed the lever. The world immediately plunged into silence and stillness. Karel was frozen, one hand reaching out in a futile attempt to catch the falling gears. Josef moved with practiced haste, stepping off the stool, gently intercepting the gears mid-air, and placing them safely back on the workbench. He then subtly nudged Karel's polishing cloth a fraction of an inch further, making it appear as though the apprentice had simply paused in his work. Five seconds later, the world resumed. The gears were safe, Karel blinked, looking confused, and Josef merely cleared his throat. \"Careful there, Karel,\" he said, feigning a slight wobble as he descended the stool, \"almost had a tumble.\" Karel, still a little pale, nodded, none the wiser, and continued polishing, oblivious to the near disaster, or the silent, five-second miracle that had just occurred. Josef merely smiled, a secret keeper of time's brief pause, in the heart of old Prague."}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: clockmaker_story_surface\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: clockmaker_story_surface\n      components[10]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[3]: title,story_image,story_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: title\n          text: The Clockmaker's Five Seconds\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Image\n          id: story_image\n          url: /images/prague_clock_shop_1895.png\n          variant: header\n          accessibility:\n            label: \"An old clock shop in Prague in 1895, filled with intricate clocks and gears.\"\n        - child: card_content\n          component: Card\n          id: story_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: card_content\n          children[5]: p1,p2,p3,p4,p5\n        - component: Text\n          id: p1\n          text: \"Josef Kovář, a man whose hands moved with the precision of the gears he meticulously crafted, owned a small, unassuming clock shop nestled in the labyrinthine alleys of Prague in the year 1895. His shop, \\\"Časové Kouzlo\\\" (Time's Magic), was a sanctuary of ticking, chiming, and the gentle whir of unseen mechanisms. Josef, a bachelor in his late forties, lived for the intricate dance of springs and cogs.\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Text\n          id: p2\n          text: \"One crisp autumn evening, while disassembling an antique pocket watch brought in by a reclusive count, Josef discovered a peculiar additional mechanism. It was a tiny, almost invisible lever, connected to a crystal that pulsed with a faint, otherworldly blue light when activated. Driven by an insatiable curiosity, Josef spent weeks studying it, sacrificing sleep and meals. Finally, with a trembling hand, he pressed the lever.\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Text\n          id: p3\n          text: \"The world around him froze. The pendulum of the grandfather clock in the corner hung mid-swing, a dust motes suspended in the air like tiny, frozen stars, and the distant clatter of a horse-drawn carriage from outside vanished into an absolute silence. Josef, however, could move freely. He checked his own pocket watch – exactly five seconds had passed when the world snapped back into motion, the pendulum resuming its swing with a soft 'tick-tock', the dust motes falling, and the carriage sound returning. He had stumbled upon a device that could halt time itself, for precisely five seconds. He named it the \\\"Chronos Shard.\\\"\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Text\n          id: p4\n          text: \"A week later, the Chronos Shard found its purpose. Josef was perched precariously on a tall stool, reaching for a rare, gilded cuckoo clock on a high shelf. Below him, his young apprentice, Karel, was meticulously polishing a display case filled with delicate porcelain figurines. As Josef stretched, his elbow accidentally nudged a stack of finely crafted wooden gears he had left on the edge of his workbench. They teetered, threatening to cascade down onto Karel and the fragile porcelain below. A scream caught in Karel's throat as he looked up, eyes wide with horror.\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Text\n          id: p5\n          text: \"Without a moment's hesitation, Josef's hand flew to his waistcoat pocket, retrieving the Chronos Shard. He pressed the lever. The world immediately plunged into silence and stillness. Karel was frozen, one hand reaching out in a futile attempt to catch the falling gears. Josef moved with practiced haste, stepping off the stool, gently intercepting the gears mid-air, and placing them safely back on the workbench. He then subtly nudged Karel's polishing cloth a fraction of an inch further, making it appear as though the apprentice had simply paused in his work. Five seconds later, the world resumed. The gears were safe, Karel blinked, looking confused, and Josef merely cleared his throat. \\\"Careful there, Karel,\\\" he said, feigning a slight wobble as he descended the stool, \\\"almost had a tumble.\\\" Karel, still a little pale, nodded, none the wiser, and continued polishing, oblivious to the near disaster, or the silent, five-second miracle that had just occurred. Josef merely smiled, a secret keeper of time's brief pause, in the heart of old Prague.\"\n          variant: body","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.1,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":619,"output_tokens_json":612,"component_count":10.0,"unique_component_types":4.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.6,"container_to_text_ratio":0.5,"information_chunking_score":0.6607943625880845,"ui_modularity_score":0.1,"ui_decomposition_score":0.3738255391842835,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":0.0,"intent_require_sections":0.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":0.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":1.0,"intent_score":1.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":27488.445520401,"input_tokens":14671,"output_tokens":1254,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:26:30.010632Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000442_01","response_id":"r_000442_01","query_id":"q_000442","intent":"Creating Writing","tags":["character creation","cyberpunk","world building"],"intent_bucket":"creative_writing","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"character_profile_surface_1","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateDataModel":{"surfaceId":"character_profile_surface_1","path":"/","value":{"name":"Kaito \"Ghost\" Ishikawa","age":24,"physicalDescription":"Kaito stands at a lean 170 cm, a wiry frame honed by countless hours navigating Neo-Tokyo's crowded alleyways and rooftops. His short, dark hair is often slicked back with sweat and rain, framing a sharp, angular face dominated by piercing, dark brown eyes that constantly dart, scanning his surroundings. A faint, jagged scar runs from his left temple down to his cheekbone, a memento from a botched data retrieval. He typically wears a worn, reinforced trench coat over dark, utilitarian clothing, pockets bulging with various data chips and tools. His movements are fluid, almost silent, a necessity for his line of work, often cloaked in the shadows of the city's neon glow.","occupation":"Freelance Data Courier in Neo-Tokyo","enhancement":{"name":"Neural Synapse Accelerator (NSA)","description":"Implanted directly into his cerebral cortex, the NSA is a highly illegal, experimental neural processor that drastically speeds up Kaito's cognitive functions and reaction times for short bursts. When activated, his perception of time slows, allowing him to process vast amounts of data, analyze complex situations, or react to threats with superhuman speed. It's not a combat augmentation in the traditional sense, but it gives him an unparalleled edge in data decryption, system bypassing, and evasive maneuvers during high-stakes runs. The drawback: prolonged use leads to severe neural strain, disorientation, and a crushing 'crash' afterwards, often accompanied by intense migraines, temporary sensory overload, and even memory gaps. It's a high-risk, high-reward tool he uses sparingly, knowing each activation brings him closer to its irreversible neurological tolls."},"backstory":"Kaito grew up in the shadow of Neo-Tokyo's towering arcologies, a digital native from the grimy lower sectors where data streams were as vital as air. His family, burdened by mounting medical debt from his younger sister's rare genetic illness, pushed him towards a corporate track, but Kaito found the structured life stifling. Instead, he gravitated to the underground, honing his natural aptitude for data manipulation and urban navigation. He started small, running encrypted messages for local fixers, quickly earning the moniker \"Ghost\" for his uncanny ability to disappear into the city's labyrinthine networks and physical spaces, always delivering.\n\nHis downfall began with a seemingly routine job: delivering a package of sensitive corporate schematics across the city. The client was a mid-tier yakuza lieutenant, 'Ryu,' from the notorious Crimson Coil Syndicate. Kaito, confident in his skills, accepted without his usual rigorous vetting, seduced by the exorbitant pay. Mid-delivery, he was ambushed by a rival gang, the 'Neon Serpents,' who had been tipped off to the high-value data. Kaito managed to escape with the package, but not before a brutal chase through the Shinjuku slums that ended with the package being severely damaged – data corrupted beyond retrieval.\n\nRyu was not pleased. The schematics were crucial to a planned corporate takeover, and their loss cost the Crimson Coil millions in potential profits and street cred. Instead of simply eliminating Kaito, Ryu, impressed by the courier's tenacity in escaping, offered a 'deal.' Kaito would work off the colossal debt – estimated at 50 million yen – through high-risk, off-the-books data runs and information gathering, directly for the syndicate. His life, and the safety of his remaining family, now hung by a thread, contingent on his unwavering service to the Crimson Coil. Every delivery, every hack, every whisper of information he gathers isn't just a job; it's another chip away at a debt that feels like a digital shackle, binding him to the city's darkest corners."}}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"character_profile_surface_1","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["main_card"]},{"id":"main_card","component":"Card","child":"card_content"},{"id":"card_content","component":"Column","children":["character_name","main_tabs"]},{"id":"character_name","component":"Text","variant":"h1","text":{"path":"/name"}},{"id":"main_tabs","component":"Tabs","tabs":[{"title":"Profile","child":"profile_tab_content"},{"title":"Cybernetic Enhancement","child":"enhancement_tab_content"},{"title":"Backstory","child":"backstory_tab_content"}]},{"id":"profile_tab_content","component":"Column","children":["age_row","occupation_row","divider_1","phys_desc_header","phys_desc_text"]},{"id":"age_row","component":"Row","align":"center","children":["age_label","age_value"]},{"id":"age_label","component":"Text","variant":"h5","text":"Age: "},{"id":"age_value","component":"Text","text":{"path":"/age"}},{"id":"occupation_row","component":"Row","align":"center","children":["occupation_label","occupation_value"]},{"id":"occupation_label","component":"Text","variant":"h5","text":"Occupation: "},{"id":"occupation_value","component":"Text","text":{"path":"/occupation"}},{"id":"divider_1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"phys_desc_header","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Physical Description"},{"id":"phys_desc_text","component":"Text","text":{"path":"/physicalDescription"}},{"id":"enhancement_tab_content","component":"Column","children":["enhancement_name","enhancement_desc"]},{"id":"enhancement_name","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":{"path":"/enhancement/name"}},{"id":"enhancement_desc","component":"Text","text":{"path":"/enhancement/description"}},{"id":"backstory_tab_content","component":"Column","children":["backstory_header","backstory_text"]},{"id":"backstory_header","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Backstory"},{"id":"backstory_text","component":"Text","text":{"path":"/backstory"}}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[3]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: character_profile_surface_1\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateDataModel:\n      path: /\n      surfaceId: character_profile_surface_1\n      value:\n        age: 24\n        backstory: \"Kaito grew up in the shadow of Neo-Tokyo's towering arcologies, a digital native from the grimy lower sectors where data streams were as vital as air. His family, burdened by mounting medical debt from his younger sister's rare genetic illness, pushed him towards a corporate track, but Kaito found the structured life stifling. Instead, he gravitated to the underground, honing his natural aptitude for data manipulation and urban navigation. He started small, running encrypted messages for local fixers, quickly earning the moniker \\\"Ghost\\\" for his uncanny ability to disappear into the city's labyrinthine networks and physical spaces, always delivering.\\n\\nHis downfall began with a seemingly routine job: delivering a package of sensitive corporate schematics across the city. The client was a mid-tier yakuza lieutenant, 'Ryu,' from the notorious Crimson Coil Syndicate. Kaito, confident in his skills, accepted without his usual rigorous vetting, seduced by the exorbitant pay. Mid-delivery, he was ambushed by a rival gang, the 'Neon Serpents,' who had been tipped off to the high-value data. Kaito managed to escape with the package, but not before a brutal chase through the Shinjuku slums that ended with the package being severely damaged – data corrupted beyond retrieval.\\n\\nRyu was not pleased. The schematics were crucial to a planned corporate takeover, and their loss cost the Crimson Coil millions in potential profits and street cred. Instead of simply eliminating Kaito, Ryu, impressed by the courier's tenacity in escaping, offered a 'deal.' Kaito would work off the colossal debt – estimated at 50 million yen – through high-risk, off-the-books data runs and information gathering, directly for the syndicate. His life, and the safety of his remaining family, now hung by a thread, contingent on his unwavering service to the Crimson Coil. Every delivery, every hack, every whisper of information he gathers isn't just a job; it's another chip away at a debt that feels like a digital shackle, binding him to the city's darkest corners.\"\n        name: \"Kaito \\\"Ghost\\\" Ishikawa\"\n        occupation: Freelance Data Courier in Neo-Tokyo\n        physicalDescription: \"Kaito stands at a lean 170 cm, a wiry frame honed by countless hours navigating Neo-Tokyo's crowded alleyways and rooftops. His short, dark hair is often slicked back with sweat and rain, framing a sharp, angular face dominated by piercing, dark brown eyes that constantly dart, scanning his surroundings. A faint, jagged scar runs from his left temple down to his cheekbone, a memento from a botched data retrieval. He typically wears a worn, reinforced trench coat over dark, utilitarian clothing, pockets bulging with various data chips and tools. His movements are fluid, almost silent, a necessity for his line of work, often cloaked in the shadows of the city's neon glow.\"\n        enhancement:\n          description: \"Implanted directly into his cerebral cortex, the NSA is a highly illegal, experimental neural processor that drastically speeds up Kaito's cognitive functions and reaction times for short bursts. When activated, his perception of time slows, allowing him to process vast amounts of data, analyze complex situations, or react to threats with superhuman speed. It's not a combat augmentation in the traditional sense, but it gives him an unparalleled edge in data decryption, system bypassing, and evasive maneuvers during high-stakes runs. The drawback: prolonged use leads to severe neural strain, disorientation, and a crushing 'crash' afterwards, often accompanied by intense migraines, temporary sensory overload, and even memory gaps. It's a high-risk, high-reward tool he uses sparingly, knowing each activation brings him closer to its irreversible neurological tolls.\"\n          name: Neural Synapse Accelerator (NSA)\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: character_profile_surface_1\n      components[21]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[1]: main_card\n        - child: card_content\n          component: Card\n          id: main_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: card_content\n          children[2]: character_name,main_tabs\n        - component: Text\n          id: character_name\n          variant: h1\n          text:\n            path: /name\n        - component: Tabs\n          id: main_tabs\n          tabs[3]{child,title}:\n            profile_tab_content,Profile\n            enhancement_tab_content,Cybernetic Enhancement\n            backstory_tab_content,Backstory\n        - component: Column\n          id: profile_tab_content\n          children[5]: age_row,occupation_row,divider_1,phys_desc_header,phys_desc_text\n        - align: center\n          component: Row\n          id: age_row\n          children[2]: age_label,age_value\n        - component: Text\n          id: age_label\n          text: \"Age: \"\n          variant: h5\n        - component: Text\n          id: age_value\n          text:\n            path: /age\n        - align: center\n          component: Row\n          id: occupation_row\n          children[2]: occupation_label,occupation_value\n        - component: Text\n          id: occupation_label\n          text: \"Occupation: \"\n          variant: h5\n        - component: Text\n          id: occupation_value\n          text:\n            path: /occupation\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: phys_desc_header\n          text: Physical Description\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: phys_desc_text\n          text:\n            path: /physicalDescription\n        - component: Column\n          id: enhancement_tab_content\n          children[2]: enhancement_name,enhancement_desc\n        - component: Text\n          id: enhancement_name\n          variant: h3\n          text:\n            path: /enhancement/name\n        - component: Text\n          id: enhancement_desc\n          text:\n            path: /enhancement/description\n        - component: Column\n          id: backstory_tab_content\n          children[2]: backstory_header,backstory_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: backstory_header\n          text: Backstory\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Text\n          id: backstory_text\n          text:\n            path: /backstory","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9721448467966574,"dup_rate":0.12578616352201258,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":779,"output_tokens_json":772,"component_count":21.0,"unique_component_types":6.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.5714285714285714,"container_to_text_ratio":0.8181818181818182,"information_chunking_score":0.8371040723981901,"ui_modularity_score":0.14285714285714285,"ui_decomposition_score":0.5440441911030147,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.16666666666666666,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":0.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":0.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":40039.00980949402,"input_tokens":14836,"output_tokens":2046,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:27:11.113210Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000462_01","response_id":"r_000462_01","query_id":"q_000462","intent":"Creating Writing","tags":["mystery","plot outline","historical fiction"],"intent_bucket":"creative_writing","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"celestialExpressMystery","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"celestialExpressMystery","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["main_title","setting_card","victim_card","weapon_card","suspects_card","twist_card"]},{"id":"main_title","component":"Text","variant":"h1","text":"The Celestial Express Mystery"},{"id":"setting_card","component":"Card","child":"setting_content"},{"id":"setting_content","component":"Column","children":["setting_title","setting_body"]},{"id":"setting_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Setting"},{"id":"setting_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"The year is 1935. The journey unfolds aboard \"The Celestial Express,\" a lavish, trans-European luxury train, as it makes its celebrated five-day voyage from the Gare de Lyon in Paris to the Sirkeci Terminal in Istanbul. The train is a moving palace of polished wood, brass, and velvet, filled with an eclectic mix of European aristocracy, industrialists, artists, and spies, all confined within its luxurious carriages as it speeds across picturesque landscapes and through bustling cities."},{"id":"victim_card","component":"Card","child":"victim_content"},{"id":"victim_content","component":"Column","children":["victim_title","victim_body"]},{"id":"victim_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Victim"},{"id":"victim_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Baroness Eleanor Dubois. A formidable and famously ruthless French industrialist, known for her sharp wit, scandalous past, and a reputation for crushing rivals without mercy. She is found dead in her lavish private compartment, appearing to have died peacefully in her sleep. However, a closer inspection reveals a tiny, almost invisible puncture mark on her neck."},{"id":"weapon_card","component":"Card","child":"weapon_content"},{"id":"weapon_content","component":"Column","children":["weapon_title","weapon_body"]},{"id":"weapon_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Murder Weapon"},{"id":"weapon_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"A small, poisoned hatpin. The pin, intricately decorated with a faux pearl, was custom-made and coated with a fast-acting, undetectable neurotoxin. It was likely administered during a brief, close encounter, leaving minimal evidence."},{"id":"suspects_card","component":"Card","child":"suspects_content"},{"id":"suspects_content","component":"Column","children":["suspects_title","suspect1_title","suspect1_body","divider1","suspect2_title","suspect2_body","divider2","suspect3_title","suspect3_body"]},{"id":"suspects_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Suspects and Motives"},{"id":"suspect1_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Suspect 1: Monsieur Antoine Dubois"},{"id":"suspect1_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Motive: Financial Ruin and Revenge. Antoine is the Baroness's estranged nephew, recently disinherited after his failing art gallery was refused a crucial loan by his aunt. He is desperate, facing bankruptcy, and believes the Baroness deliberately sabotaged his attempts to secure funding, driven by her disdain for his lifestyle. He stands to inherit a substantial sum upon her death, despite the disinheritance, due to a clause in an older will."},{"id":"divider1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"suspect2_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Suspect 2: Lady Beatrice Finch"},{"id":"suspect2_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Motive: Long-held Grudge and Social Retribution. Lady Beatrice is a seemingly demure English socialite whose prominent family suffered a devastating financial collapse years ago, directly attributable to a hostile takeover orchestrated by Baroness Dubois. Lady Beatrice's family was publicly shamed and impoverished, and she has carried a quiet, simmering resentment, seeking an opportunity for retribution against the woman who ruined her family's standing."},{"id":"divider2","component":"Divider"},{"id":"suspect3_title","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Suspect 3: Dr. Alistair Reed"},{"id":"suspect3_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Motive: Professional Integrity and Protection of Legacy. Dr. Reed is a renowned British archaeologist traveling with a newly discovered, invaluable ancient artifact that the Baroness had publicly and aggressively attempted to acquire through highly questionable means. Her tactics threatened to discredit Dr. Reed's reputation and research, potentially leading to the artifact being seized and misused. He feared she would stop at nothing to possess it, even resorting to theft."},{"id":"twist_card","component":"Card","child":"twist_content"},{"id":"twist_content","component":"Column","children":["twist_title","twist_body"]},{"id":"twist_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"The Plot Twist"},{"id":"twist_body","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"The true killer is Lady Beatrice Finch, but her primary motive is not personal revenge. Lady Beatrice is, in fact, an undercover agent for the British Secret Service. Baroness Dubois was secretly a key figure in an international espionage ring, planning to sell highly sensitive industrial and military secrets to a rival power during a clandestine meeting in Istanbul. Lady Beatrice was assigned to eliminate the Baroness and retrieve crucial documents hidden in the Baroness's compartment before the train reached its destination. Her family's historical grievance against the Baroness served as a perfect, believable cover for her presence and actions on the train, diverting suspicion from her true mission. The poisoned hatpin was a specialized tool developed by the Secret Service for discreet assassinations. The \"disinheritance\" of Monsieur Dubois and Dr. Reed's \"archaeological artifact\" were elaborate red herrings, carefully placed or exploited by Lady Beatrice to further obscure her real objective."}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: celestialExpressMystery\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: celestialExpressMystery\n      components[29]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[6]: main_title,setting_card,victim_card,weapon_card,suspects_card,twist_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: main_title\n          text: The Celestial Express Mystery\n          variant: h1\n        - child: setting_content\n          component: Card\n          id: setting_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: setting_content\n          children[2]: setting_title,setting_body\n        - component: Text\n          id: setting_title\n          text: Setting\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: setting_body\n          text: \"The year is 1935. The journey unfolds aboard \\\"The Celestial Express,\\\" a lavish, trans-European luxury train, as it makes its celebrated five-day voyage from the Gare de Lyon in Paris to the Sirkeci Terminal in Istanbul. The train is a moving palace of polished wood, brass, and velvet, filled with an eclectic mix of European aristocracy, industrialists, artists, and spies, all confined within its luxurious carriages as it speeds across picturesque landscapes and through bustling cities.\"\n          variant: body\n        - child: victim_content\n          component: Card\n          id: victim_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: victim_content\n          children[2]: victim_title,victim_body\n        - component: Text\n          id: victim_title\n          text: Victim\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: victim_body\n          text: \"Baroness Eleanor Dubois. A formidable and famously ruthless French industrialist, known for her sharp wit, scandalous past, and a reputation for crushing rivals without mercy. She is found dead in her lavish private compartment, appearing to have died peacefully in her sleep. However, a closer inspection reveals a tiny, almost invisible puncture mark on her neck.\"\n          variant: body\n        - child: weapon_content\n          component: Card\n          id: weapon_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: weapon_content\n          children[2]: weapon_title,weapon_body\n        - component: Text\n          id: weapon_title\n          text: Murder Weapon\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: weapon_body\n          text: \"A small, poisoned hatpin. The pin, intricately decorated with a faux pearl, was custom-made and coated with a fast-acting, undetectable neurotoxin. It was likely administered during a brief, close encounter, leaving minimal evidence.\"\n          variant: body\n        - child: suspects_content\n          component: Card\n          id: suspects_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: suspects_content\n          children[9]: suspects_title,suspect1_title,suspect1_body,divider1,suspect2_title,suspect2_body,divider2,suspect3_title,suspect3_body\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspects_title\n          text: Suspects and Motives\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect1_title\n          text: \"Suspect 1: Monsieur Antoine Dubois\"\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect1_body\n          text: \"Motive: Financial Ruin and Revenge. Antoine is the Baroness's estranged nephew, recently disinherited after his failing art gallery was refused a crucial loan by his aunt. He is desperate, facing bankruptcy, and believes the Baroness deliberately sabotaged his attempts to secure funding, driven by her disdain for his lifestyle. He stands to inherit a substantial sum upon her death, despite the disinheritance, due to a clause in an older will.\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider1\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect2_title\n          text: \"Suspect 2: Lady Beatrice Finch\"\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect2_body\n          text: \"Motive: Long-held Grudge and Social Retribution. Lady Beatrice is a seemingly demure English socialite whose prominent family suffered a devastating financial collapse years ago, directly attributable to a hostile takeover orchestrated by Baroness Dubois. Lady Beatrice's family was publicly shamed and impoverished, and she has carried a quiet, simmering resentment, seeking an opportunity for retribution against the woman who ruined her family's standing.\"\n          variant: body\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider2\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect3_title\n          text: \"Suspect 3: Dr. Alistair Reed\"\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: suspect3_body\n          text: \"Motive: Professional Integrity and Protection of Legacy. Dr. Reed is a renowned British archaeologist traveling with a newly discovered, invaluable ancient artifact that the Baroness had publicly and aggressively attempted to acquire through highly questionable means. Her tactics threatened to discredit Dr. Reed's reputation and research, potentially leading to the artifact being seized and misused. He feared she would stop at nothing to possess it, even resorting to theft.\"\n          variant: body\n        - child: twist_content\n          component: Card\n          id: twist_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: twist_content\n          children[2]: twist_title,twist_body\n        - component: Text\n          id: twist_title\n          text: The Plot Twist\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: twist_body\n          text: \"The true killer is Lady Beatrice Finch, but her primary motive is not personal revenge. Lady Beatrice is, in fact, an undercover agent for the British Secret Service. Baroness Dubois was secretly a key figure in an international espionage ring, planning to sell highly sensitive industrial and military secrets to a rival power during a clandestine meeting in Istanbul. Lady Beatrice was assigned to eliminate the Baroness and retrieve crucial documents hidden in the Baroness's compartment before the train reached its destination. Her family's historical grievance against the Baroness served as a perfect, believable cover for her presence and actions on the train, diverting suspicion from her true mission. The poisoned hatpin was a specialized tool developed by the Secret Service for discreet assassinations. The \\\"disinheritance\\\" of Monsieur Dubois and Dr. Reed's \\\"archaeological artifact\\\" were elaborate red herrings, carefully placed or exploited by Lady Beatrice to further obscure her real objective.\"\n          variant: body","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9695121951219512,"dup_rate":0.22424242424242424,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":778,"output_tokens_json":763,"component_count":29.0,"unique_component_types":4.0,"max_tree_depth":4.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.6206896551724137,"container_to_text_ratio":0.6875,"information_chunking_score":0.7239213544511196,"ui_modularity_score":0.1724137931034483,"ui_decomposition_score":0.44830438583275267,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":1.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":0.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":0.0,"intent_sections_ok":1.0,"intent_expectation_pass":1.0,"intent_score":1.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":36339.120864868164,"input_tokens":14779,"output_tokens":2061,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:27:48.547786Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000481_01","response_id":"r_000481_01","query_id":"q_000481","intent":"Event Schedule","tags":["corporate","itinerary","workshop"],"intent_bucket":"event_schedule","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000481","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000481","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"Corporate Leadership Workshop Itinerary\nDate: 2024-11-15\nLocation: Chicago, USA\nStart Time: 08:30\nEnd Time: 17:00\n\nAssumptions:\n- All attendees participate in all three breakout sessions sequentially.\n- Specific content for each session is illustrative and can be customized by the organizers.\n- Breaks are 15 minutes to allow for participant refreshment and room transitions.\n- An \"Interactive Leadership Challenge\" session is included to provide practical application and enhance engagement.\n- Room assignments are optimized for the flow of a single cohort through the workshop.\n\nIcons:\n- Time: https://example.com/icons/clock.png\n- Keynote: https://example.com/icons/megaphone","variant":"body"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: workshopItinerarySurface\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: workshopItinerarySurface\n      components[1]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[1]: mainTitle","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":["{'version': 'v0.9', 'createSurface': {'surfaceId': 'workshopItinerarySurface', 'catalogId': 'https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json'}} is not of type 'array'\n\nFailed validating 'type' in schema:\n    {'$schema': 'https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema',\n     '$id': 'https:...","manual_stage4_render_repair_missing_child_component"],"repair_attempts":1,"repair_needed":true},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.09523809523809523,"dup_rate":0.125,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":23,"output_tokens_json":19,"component_count":1.0,"unique_component_types":1.0,"max_tree_depth":1.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.0,"container_to_text_ratio":1.0,"information_chunking_score":0.0,"ui_modularity_score":0.0,"ui_decomposition_score":0.2583333333333333,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":1.0,"missing_ids_rate":1.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":0.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.5},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":62318.782329559326,"input_tokens":14158,"output_tokens":139,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:29:14.269550Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000482_01","response_id":"r_000482_01","query_id":"q_000482","intent":"Event Schedule","tags":["entertainment","festival","planning"],"intent_bucket":"event_schedule","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000482","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000482","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"Echoes of Summer Festival Schedule\n\nDates: July 11 - 13, 2025\nLocation: Austin, Texas\n\nAssumptions:\n- Each act is approximately 2 hours long, allowing for 30-minute breaks between sets for stage transitions.\n- Artist names are fictional and created to represent the requested genres (Synth-pop, Indie Rock, Folk).\n\nQuick Actions:\n[Button: Get Festival Tickets] https://www.exampletickets.com/echoesofsummer\n[Button: View Festival Map] https://www.examplefestival.com/map\n[Button: Official Festival Website] https://www.examplefestival.com\n\nDay 1: Friday, July 11, 2025\n\nMain Stage\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | The Luminous Sound    | Synth-pop\n16:30-18:30 | Desert Bloom          | Indie Rock\n19:00-21:00 | Stellar Echoes        | Synth-pop\n21:30-23:00 | Horizon Lights        | Indie Rock\n\nIndie Grove\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | Whispering Pines      | Folk\n16:30-18:30 | City Ghosts           | Indie Rock\n19:00-21:00 | Meadow Lark Ensemble  | Folk\n21:30-23:00 | Neon Trails           | Synth-pop\n\nDay 2: Saturday, July 12, 2025\n\nMain Stage\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | Electric Dawn         | Synth-pop\n16:30-18:30 | The Wandering Souls   | Folk\n19:00-21:00 | Crimson Tide          | Indie Rock\n21:30-23:00 | Cosmic Reverie        | Synth-pop\n\nIndie Grove\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | Sunstone Collective   | Indie Rock\n16:30-18:30 | Riverbend Duo         | Folk\n19:00-21:00 | Skyline Drifters      | Indie Rock\n21:30-23:00 | Echo Bloom            | Folk\n\nDay 3: Sunday, July 13, 2025\n\nMain Stage\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | Pixel Heartbeat       | Synth-pop\n16:30-18:30 | Stone Creek Ramblers  | Folk\n19:00-21:00 | The Velvet Static     | Indie Rock\n21:30-23:00 | Dream Weaver          | Synth-pop\n\nIndie Grove\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\n------------------------------------------------\n14:00-16:00 | Forest Canopy         | Folk\n16:30-18:30 | Juniper Roots         | Indie Rock\n19:00-21:00 | Aurora Bloom          | Synth-pop\n21:30-23:00 | The Dusty Roads       | Folk","variant":"body"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000482\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000482\n      components[2]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[1]: text_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: text_1\n          text: \"Echoes of Summer Festival Schedule\\n\\nDates: July 11 - 13, 2025\\nLocation: Austin, Texas\\n\\nAssumptions:\\n- Each act is approximately 2 hours long, allowing for 30-minute breaks between sets for stage transitions.\\n- Artist names are fictional and created to represent the requested genres (Synth-pop, Indie Rock, Folk).\\n\\nQuick Actions:\\n[Button: Get Festival Tickets] https://www.exampletickets.com/echoesofsummer\\n[Button: View Festival Map] https://www.examplefestival.com/map\\n[Button: Official Festival Website] https://www.examplefestival.com\\n\\nDay 1: Friday, July 11, 2025\\n\\nMain Stage\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | The Luminous Sound    | Synth-pop\\n16:30-18:30 | Desert Bloom          | Indie Rock\\n19:00-21:00 | Stellar Echoes        | Synth-pop\\n21:30-23:00 | Horizon Lights        | Indie Rock\\n\\nIndie Grove\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | Whispering Pines      | Folk\\n16:30-18:30 | City Ghosts           | Indie Rock\\n19:00-21:00 | Meadow Lark Ensemble  | Folk\\n21:30-23:00 | Neon Trails           | Synth-pop\\n\\nDay 2: Saturday, July 12, 2025\\n\\nMain Stage\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | Electric Dawn         | Synth-pop\\n16:30-18:30 | The Wandering Souls   | Folk\\n19:00-21:00 | Crimson Tide          | Indie Rock\\n21:30-23:00 | Cosmic Reverie        | Synth-pop\\n\\nIndie Grove\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | Sunstone Collective   | Indie Rock\\n16:30-18:30 | Riverbend Duo         | Folk\\n19:00-21:00 | Skyline Drifters      | Indie Rock\\n21:30-23:00 | Echo Bloom            | Folk\\n\\nDay 3: Sunday, July 13, 2025\\n\\nMain Stage\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | Pixel Heartbeat       | Synth-pop\\n16:30-18:30 | Stone Creek Ramblers  | Folk\\n19:00-21:00 | The Velvet Static     | Indie Rock\\n21:30-23:00 | Dream Weaver          | Synth-pop\\n\\nIndie Grove\\nTime       | Artist Name           | Genre\\n------------------------------------------------\\n14:00-16:00 | Forest Canopy         | Folk\\n16:30-18:30 | Juniper Roots         | Indie Rock\\n19:00-21:00 | Aurora Bloom          | Synth-pop\\n21:30-23:00 | The Dusty Roads       | Folk\"\n          variant: body","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid