:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://example.com/kitchen-designs\"","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.33476394849785407,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":514,"output_tokens_json":495,"component_count":51.0,"unique_component_types":6.0,"max_tree_depth":6.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.5098039215686274,"container_to_text_ratio":0.34285714285714286,"information_chunking_score":0.7420333839150228,"ui_modularity_score":0.1568627450980392,"ui_decomposition_score":0.4176223630575144,"actionable_elements":3.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.05405405405405406,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.3333333333333333},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":45688.14253807068,"input_tokens":14353,"output_tokens":2897,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:31:56.107965Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000521_01","response_id":"r_000521_01","query_id":"q_000521","intent":"Research Analysis","tags":["finance","historical analysis","market research"],"intent_bucket":"research_analysis","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"finance_comparison_surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json","theme":{"iconUrl":"/icons/finance.png"}}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"finance_comparison_surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["assumptions_text","summary_card","volatility_card","overview_card","crashes_card","actions_row"]},{"id":"assumptions_text","component":"Text","variant":"caption","text":"Assumptions: All data provided is illustrative and based on general historical trends for the specified period (January 1, 2000, to December 31, 2020). Actual returns and volatility may vary based on specific data sources and calculation methodologies."},{"id":"summary_card","component":"Card","child":"summary_col"},{"id":"summary_col","component":"Column","children":["summary_title","summary_intro","summary_sp500","summary_gold"]},{"id":"summary_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Summary of Performance (EXAMPLE DATA)"},{"id":"summary_intro","component":"Text","text":"During the period from January 1, 2000, to December 31, 2020, both the S&P 500 and Gold experienced significant growth, but with differing trajectories and overall returns."},{"id":"summary_sp500","component":"Text","text":"• S&P 500: The S&P 500, representing a broad measure of U.S. equities, navigated through two major bear markets (dot-com bust and 2008 financial crisis) before a strong bull run. Its total percentage growth (price return, excluding dividends) was approximately +175%."},{"id":"summary_gold","component":"Text","text":"• Gold: Often considered a safe-haven asset, Gold saw substantial appreciation, particularly during periods of economic uncertainty and low interest rates. Its total percentage growth was approximately +420%."},{"id":"volatility_card","component":"Card","child":"volatility_col"},{"id":"volatility_col","component":"Column","children":["volatility_title","volatility_intro","volatility_sp500","volatility_gold","volatility_conclusion"]},{"id":"volatility_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Volatility Comparison (EXAMPLE DATA)"},{"id":"volatility_intro","component":"Text","text":"Volatility refers to the degree of variation of a trading price series over time. Higher volatility implies greater price swings."},{"id":"volatility_sp500","component":"Text","text":"• S&P 500: Experienced significant periods of high volatility, particularly during market downturns like the dot-com bust (2000-2002), the Global Financial Crisis (2008-2009), and the COVID-19 crash (2020). The S&P 500 generally exhibited higher volatility over this period."},{"id":"volatility_gold","component":"Text","text":"• Gold: While Gold can also be volatile, it often demonstrated a lower correlation with equities and sometimes acted as a hedge during equity market downturns. However, it also had its own periods of significant price swings, especially after major rallies."},{"id":"volatility_conclusion","component":"Text","text":"Conclusion on Volatility: The S&P 500 generally had higher volatility due to the more pronounced and frequent large drawdowns it experienced during this specific timeframe."},{"id":"overview_card","component":"Card","child":"overview_col"},{"id":"overview_col","component":"Column","children":["overview_title","overview_header_row","overview_divider_1","overview_sp500_row","overview_divider_2","overview_gold_row"]},{"id":"overview_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Performance and Volatility Overview (EXAMPLE DATA)"},{"id":"overview_header_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["header_asset","header_growth","header_volatility"]},{"id":"header_asset","component":"Text","text":"Asset","weight":1},{"id":"header_growth","component":"Text","text":"Total Growth (Jan 2000 - Dec 2020)","weight":1},{"id":"header_volatility","component":"Text","text":"Volatility Level","weight":1},{"id":"overview_divider_1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"overview_sp500_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["sp500_asset","sp500_growth","sp500_volatility"]},{"id":"sp500_asset","component":"Text","text":"S&P 500","weight":1},{"id":"sp500_growth","component":"Text","text":"+175%","weight":1},{"id":"sp500_volatility","component":"Text","text":"Higher","weight":1},{"id":"overview_divider_2","component":"Divider"},{"id":"overview_gold_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["gold_asset","gold_growth","gold_volatility"]},{"id":"gold_asset","component":"Text","text":"Gold","weight":1},{"id":"gold_growth","component":"Text","text":"+420%","weight":1},{"id":"gold_volatility","component":"Text","text":"Moderate","weight":1},{"id":"crashes_card","component":"Card","child":"crashes_col"},{"id":"crashes_col","component":"Column","children":["crashes_title","crashes_item1","crashes_item2","crashes_item3"]},{"id":"crashes_title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Significant Market Crashes (January 1, 2000 - December 31, 2020)"},{"id":"crashes_item1","component":"Text","text":"1. Dot-com Bubble Burst (2000-2002): While starting prior to 2000, the full impact of the collapse of the technology and internet bubble was deeply felt in the early 2000s, leading to a significant bear market for the S&P 500."},{"id":"crashes_item2","component":"Text","text":"2. Global Financial Crisis (2008): Triggered by the subprime mortgage crisis, this led to a severe worldwide economic recession and one of the largest stock market crashes in history, with the S&P 500 dropping over 50% from its peak."},{"id":"crashes_item3","component":"Text","text":"3. COVID-19 Market Crash (Early 2020): A rapid and severe global stock market decline in February-March 2020, caused by the emerging COVID-19 pandemic and the resulting economic lockdowns and uncertainty."},{"id":"actions_row","component":"Row","justify":"start","children":["sp500_button","gold_button"]},{"id":"sp500_button","component":"Button","child":"sp500_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.spglobal.com/spdji/en/indices/equity/sp-500/"}}}},{"id":"sp500_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Learn more about S&P 500"},{"id":"gold_button","component":"Button","child":"gold_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://www.gold.org/"}}}},{"id":"gold_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Explore Gold as an investment"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: finance_comparison_surface\n      theme:\n        iconUrl: /icons/finance.png\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: finance_comparison_surface\n      components[43]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[6]: assumptions_text,summary_card,volatility_card,overview_card,crashes_card,actions_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_text\n          text: \"Assumptions: All data provided is illustrative and based on general historical trends for the specified period (January 1, 2000, to December 31, 2020). Actual returns and volatility may vary based on specific data sources and calculation methodologies.\"\n          variant: caption\n        - child: summary_col\n          component: Card\n          id: summary_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: summary_col\n          children[4]: summary_title,summary_intro,summary_sp500,summary_gold\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_title\n          text: Summary of Performance (EXAMPLE DATA)\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_intro\n          text: \"During the period from January 1, 2000, to December 31, 2020, both the S&P 500 and Gold experienced significant growth, but with differing trajectories and overall returns.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_sp500\n          text: \"• S&P 500: The S&P 500, representing a broad measure of U.S. equities, navigated through two major bear markets (dot-com bust and 2008 financial crisis) before a strong bull run. Its total percentage growth (price return, excluding dividends) was approximately +175%.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_gold\n          text: \"• Gold: Often considered a safe-haven asset, Gold saw substantial appreciation, particularly during periods of economic uncertainty and low interest rates. Its total percentage growth was approximately +420%.\"\n        - child: volatility_col\n          component: Card\n          id: volatility_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: volatility_col\n          children[5]: volatility_title,volatility_intro,volatility_sp500,volatility_gold,volatility_conclusion\n        - component: Text\n          id: volatility_title\n          text: Volatility Comparison (EXAMPLE DATA)\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: volatility_intro\n          text: Volatility refers to the degree of variation of a trading price series over time. Higher volatility implies greater price swings.\n        - component: Text\n          id: volatility_sp500\n          text: \"• S&P 500: Experienced significant periods of high volatility, particularly during market downturns like the dot-com bust (2000-2002), the Global Financial Crisis (2008-2009), and the COVID-19 crash (2020). The S&P 500 generally exhibited higher volatility over this period.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: volatility_gold\n          text: \"• Gold: While Gold can also be volatile, it often demonstrated a lower correlation with equities and sometimes acted as a hedge during equity market downturns. However, it also had its own periods of significant price swings, especially after major rallies.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: volatility_conclusion\n          text: \"Conclusion on Volatility: The S&P 500 generally had higher volatility due to the more pronounced and frequent large drawdowns it experienced during this specific timeframe.\"\n        - child: overview_col\n          component: Card\n          id: overview_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: overview_col\n          children[6]: overview_title,overview_header_row,overview_divider_1,overview_sp500_row,overview_divider_2,overview_gold_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: overview_title\n          text: Performance and Volatility Overview (EXAMPLE DATA)\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Row\n          id: overview_header_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[3]: header_asset,header_growth,header_volatility\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_asset\n          text: Asset\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_growth\n          text: Total Growth (Jan 2000 - Dec 2020)\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_volatility\n          text: Volatility Level\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Divider\n          id: overview_divider_1\n        - component: Row\n          id: overview_sp500_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[3]: sp500_asset,sp500_growth,sp500_volatility\n        - component: Text\n          id: sp500_asset\n          text: S&P 500\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: sp500_growth\n          text: +175%\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: sp500_volatility\n          text: Higher\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Divider\n          id: overview_divider_2\n        - component: Row\n          id: overview_gold_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[3]: gold_asset,gold_growth,gold_volatility\n        - component: Text\n          id: gold_asset\n          text: Gold\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: gold_growth\n          text: +420%\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: gold_volatility\n          text: Moderate\n          weight: 1\n        - child: crashes_col\n          component: Card\n          id: crashes_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: crashes_col\n          children[4]: crashes_title,crashes_item1,crashes_item2,crashes_item3\n        - component: Text\n          id: crashes_title\n          text: \"Significant Market Crashes (January 1, 2000 - December 31, 2020)\"\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: crashes_item1\n          text: \"1. Dot-com Bubble Burst (2000-2002): While starting prior to 2000, the full impact of the collapse of the technology and internet bubble was deeply felt in the early 2000s, leading to a significant bear market for the S&P 500.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: crashes_item2\n          text: \"2. Global Financial Crisis (2008): Triggered by the subprime mortgage crisis, this led to a severe worldwide economic recession and one of the largest stock market crashes in history, with the S&P 500 dropping over 50% from its peak.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: crashes_item3\n          text: \"3. COVID-19 Market Crash (Early 2020): A rapid and severe global stock market decline in February-March 2020, caused by the emerging COVID-19 pandemic and the resulting economic lockdowns and uncertainty.\"\n        - component: Row\n          id: actions_row\n          justify: start\n          children[2]: sp500_button,gold_button\n        - child: sp500_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: sp500_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.spglobal.com/spdji/en/indices/equity/sp-500/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: sp500_button_text\n          text: Learn more about S&P 500\n        - child: gold_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: gold_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://www.gold.org/\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: gold_button_text\n          text: Explore Gold as an investment","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9950248756218906,"dup_rate":0.2548076923076923,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":757,"output_tokens_json":738,"component_count":43.0,"unique_component_types":6.0,"max_tree_depth":5.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.5813953488372092,"container_to_text_ratio":0.5,"information_chunking_score":0.8994126284875184,"ui_modularity_score":0.18604651162790697,"ui_decomposition_score":0.4930608202711471,"actionable_elements":2.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.0,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.0,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":1.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":1.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.3333333333333333},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":33658.19835662842,"input_tokens":14772,"output_tokens":2801,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:32:30.894970Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000522_01","response_id":"r_000522_01","query_id":"q_000522","intent":"Research Analysis","tags":["health","nutrition","comparative analysis"],"intent_bucket":"research_analysis","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"nutritional-comparison-surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"nutritional-comparison-surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["title","assumptions","table_title","table_card"]},{"id":"title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":"Leafy Green Nutritional Profile"},{"id":"assumptions","component":"Text","variant":"caption","text":"Assumptions:\n- Nutritional data is based on standard raw values for 100g portions.\n- Vitamin A is reported as Retinol Activity Equivalents (RAE)."},{"id":"table_card","component":"Card","child":"table_column"},{"id":"table_column","component":"Column","children":["table_header_row","divider_1","kale_row","spinach_row","chard_row"]},{"id":"table_header_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["header_green","header_calories","header_vit_a","header_vit_k","header_vit_c","header_calcium"]},{"id":"header_green","component":"Text","text":"Leafy Green","variant":"h5","weight":2},{"id":"header_calories","component":"Text","text":"Calories (kcal)","variant":"h5","weight":1},{"id":"header_vit_a","component":"Text","text":"Vitamin A (mcg RAE)","variant":"h5","weight":1},{"id":"header_vit_k","component":"Text","text":"Vitamin K (mcg)","variant":"h5","weight":1},{"id":"header_vit_c","component":"Text","text":"Vitamin C (mg)","variant":"h5","weight":1},{"id":"header_calcium","component":"Text","text":"Calcium (mg)","variant":"h5","weight":1},{"id":"divider_1","component":"Divider"},{"id":"kale_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["kale_name","kale_calories","kale_vit_a","kale_vit_k","kale_vit_c","kale_calcium"]},{"id":"kale_name","component":"Text","text":"Kale","weight":2},{"id":"kale_calories","component":"Text","text":"49","weight":1},{"id":"kale_vit_a","component":"Text","text":"500","weight":1},{"id":"kale_vit_k","component":"Text","text":"389.8","weight":1},{"id":"kale_vit_c","component":"Text","text":"120","weight":1},{"id":"kale_calcium","component":"Text","text":"150","weight":1},{"id":"spinach_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["spinach_name","spinach_calories","spinach_vit_a","spinach_vit_k","spinach_vit_c","spinach_calcium"]},{"id":"spinach_name","component":"Text","text":"Spinach","weight":2},{"id":"spinach_calories","component":"Text","text":"23","weight":1},{"id":"spinach_vit_a","component":"Text","text":"469","weight":1},{"id":"spinach_vit_k","component":"Text","text":"482.9","weight":1},{"id":"spinach_vit_c","component":"Text","text":"28.1","weight":1},{"id":"spinach_calcium","component":"Text","text":"99","weight":1},{"id":"chard_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceBetween","children":["chard_name","chard_calories","chard_vit_a","chard_vit_k","chard_vit_c","chard_calcium"]},{"id":"chard_name","component":"Text","text":"Swiss Chard","weight":2},{"id":"chard_calories","component":"Text","text":"19","weight":1},{"id":"chard_vit_a","component":"Text","text":"306","weight":1},{"id":"chard_vit_k","component":"Text","text":"830","weight":1},{"id":"chard_vit_c","component":"Text","text":"18","weight":1},{"id":"chard_calcium","component":"Text","text":"51","weight":1},{"id":"table_title","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Research Summary: Most Beneficial for Bone Density"},{"id":"summary_card","component":"Card","child":"summary_column"},{"id":"summary_column","component":"Column","children":["summary_p1","summary_p2","summary_p3"]},{"id":"summary_p1","component":"Text","text":"Based on the values provided, all three leafy greens offer valuable nutrients for bone health, but their contributions differ.\n\nCalcium is a primary structural component of bones, and Kale stands out with the highest calcium content (150 mg per 100g) among the three. Vitamin C is crucial for the synthesis of collagen, which forms the organic matrix of bone, and Kale also provides significantly more Vitamin C (120 mg) than spinach or Swiss chard."},{"id":"summary_p2","component":"Text","text":"Vitamin K plays a critical role in bone metabolism by activating proteins like osteocalcin, which helps bind calcium to the bone matrix. Swiss Chard is exceptionally rich in Vitamin K, offering 830 mcg per 100g, which is substantially higher than both Kale and Spinach. Spinach also provides a significant amount of Vitamin K (482.9 mcg)."},{"id":"summary_p3","component":"Text","text":"Considering these factors: While Swiss Chard provides the highest amount of Vitamin K, **Kale** appears to be the most beneficial for bone density based on this specific set of nutrients. It offers the highest amount of calcium (the direct building block for bones) and Vitamin C (essential for collagen formation), alongside a substantial amount of Vitamin K. This combination makes Kale a strong contender for overall bone health support by contributing to both the mineral density and the structural integrity of bones."}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: nutritional-comparison-surface\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: nutritional-comparison-surface\n      components[40]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[4]: title,assumptions,table_title,table_card\n        - component: Text\n          id: title\n          text: Leafy Green Nutritional Profile\n          variant: h2\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions\n          text: \"Assumptions:\\n- Nutritional data is based on standard raw values for 100g portions.\\n- Vitamin A is reported as Retinol Activity Equivalents (RAE).\"\n          variant: caption\n        - child: table_column\n          component: Card\n          id: table_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: table_column\n          children[5]: table_header_row,divider_1,kale_row,spinach_row,chard_row\n        - component: Row\n          id: table_header_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[6]: header_green,header_calories,header_vit_a,header_vit_k,header_vit_c,header_calcium\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_green\n          text: Leafy Green\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_calories\n          text: Calories (kcal)\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_vit_a\n          text: Vitamin A (mcg RAE)\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_vit_k\n          text: Vitamin K (mcg)\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_vit_c\n          text: Vitamin C (mg)\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: header_calcium\n          text: Calcium (mg)\n          variant: h5\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Divider\n          id: divider_1\n        - component: Row\n          id: kale_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[6]: kale_name,kale_calories,kale_vit_a,kale_vit_k,kale_vit_c,kale_calcium\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_name\n          text: Kale\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_calories\n          text: \"49\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_vit_a\n          text: \"500\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_vit_k\n          text: \"389.8\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_vit_c\n          text: \"120\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: kale_calcium\n          text: \"150\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Row\n          id: spinach_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[6]: spinach_name,spinach_calories,spinach_vit_a,spinach_vit_k,spinach_vit_c,spinach_calcium\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_name\n          text: Spinach\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_calories\n          text: \"23\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_vit_a\n          text: \"469\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_vit_k\n          text: \"482.9\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_vit_c\n          text: \"28.1\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: spinach_calcium\n          text: \"99\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Row\n          id: chard_row\n          justify: spaceBetween\n          children[6]: chard_name,chard_calories,chard_vit_a,chard_vit_k,chard_vit_c,chard_calcium\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_name\n          text: Swiss Chard\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_calories\n          text: \"19\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_vit_a\n          text: \"306\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_vit_k\n          text: \"830\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_vit_c\n          text: \"18\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: chard_calcium\n          text: \"51\"\n          weight: 1\n        - component: Text\n          id: table_title\n          text: \"Research Summary: Most Beneficial for Bone Density\"\n          variant: h3\n        - child: summary_column\n          component: Card\n          id: summary_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: summary_column\n          children[3]: summary_p1,summary_p2,summary_p3\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_p1\n          text: \"Based on the values provided, all three leafy greens offer valuable nutrients for bone health, but their contributions differ.\\n\\nCalcium is a primary structural component of bones, and Kale stands out with the highest calcium content (150 mg per 100g) among the three. Vitamin C is crucial for the synthesis of collagen, which forms the organic matrix of bone, and Kale also provides significantly more Vitamin C (120 mg) than spinach or Swiss chard.\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_p2\n          text: \"Vitamin K plays a critical role in bone metabolism by activating proteins like osteocalcin, which helps bind calcium to the bone matrix. Swiss Chard is exceptionally rich in Vitamin K, offering 830 mcg per 100g, which is substantially higher than both Kale and Spinach. Spinach also provides a significant amount of Vitamin K (482.9 mcg).\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_p3\n          text: \"Considering these factors: While Swiss Chard provides the highest amount of Vitamin K, **Kale** appears to be the most beneficial for bone density based on this specific set of nutrients. It offers the highest amount of calcium (the direct building block for bones) and Vitamin C (essential for collagen formation), alongside a substantial amount of Vitamin K. This combination makes Kale a strong contender for overall bone health support by contributing to both the mineral density and the structural integrity of bones.\"","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":1.0,"dup_rate":0.33,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":615,"output_tokens_json":601,"component_count":40.0,"unique_component_types":5.0,"max_tree_depth":5.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.4,"container_to_text_ratio":0.3,"information_chunking_score":0.6905749851807943,"ui_modularity_score":0.15,"ui_decomposition_score":0.37061499703615886,"actionable_elements":0.0,"action_coverage":1.0,"url_as_text_rate":0.0,"table_pattern_detected":0.0,"table_cell_coverage":0.0,"section_heading_coverage":0.3333333333333333,"markdown_leakage_rate":0.058823529411764705,"missing_ids":0.0,"missing_ids_rate":0.0,"dangling_components":0.0,"dangling_components_rate":0.0,"intent_require_table":1.0,"intent_require_actions":0.0,"intent_require_sections":1.0,"intent_table_ok":0.0,"intent_actions_ok":0.0,"intent_sections_ok":0.0,"intent_expectation_pass":0.0,"intent_score":0.0},"gen":{"provider":"gemini","model":"gemini-2.5-pro","prompt_version":"genui_gen_v1","latency_ms":31512.741088867188,"input_tokens":14493,"output_tokens":2372,"cost_usd":null,"error":null},"created_at":"2026-02-07T11:33:03.517971Z"}
{"ui_id":"u_000561_01","response_id":"r_000561_01","query_id":"q_000561","intent":"Comparison","tags":["health","nutrition","comparison"],"intent_bucket":"comparison","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"quinoa-vs-rice-comparison-1","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"quinoa-vs-rice-comparison-1","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["assumptions_text","summary_text","comparison_card","gi_notes_card","actions_row"]},{"id":"assumptions_text","component":"Text","variant":"caption","text":"Assumptions:\n- Nutritional values are based on 100g of cooked, plain quinoa and 100g of cooked, plain long-grain brown rice, prepared with water and no added fats or seasonings.\n- Glycemic Index (GI) values are approximate and can vary based on preparation, specific variety, and individual metabolic response."},{"id":"summary_text","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":"Summary:\nBoth cooked quinoa and cooked brown rice are nutritious whole grains, offering good sources of protein and fiber. Quinoa generally provides a higher protein and fiber content per 100g serving compared to brown rice. Their glycemic index values are similar, both falling into the moderate category."},{"id":"comparison_card","component":"Card","child":"comparison_column"},{"id":"comparison_column","component":"Column","children":["comparison_header","table_header_row","table_divider","protein_row","fiber_row","gi_row"]},{"id":"comparison_header","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Nutritional Comparison (per 100g cooked)"},{"id":"table_header_row","component":"Row","children":["nutrient_header_text","quinoa_header_text","rice_header_text"]},{"id":"nutrient_header_text","component":"Text","text":"Nutrient","weight":2},{"id":"quinoa_header_text","component":"Text","text":"Cooked Quinoa (100g)","weight":1.5},{"id":"rice_header_text","component":"Text","text":"Cooked Brown Rice (100g)","weight":1.5},{"id":"table_divider","component":"Divider"},{"id":"protein_row","component":"Row","children":["protein_label_text","protein_quinoa_text","protein_rice_text"]},{"id":"protein_label_text","component":"Text","text":"Protein","weight":2},{"id":"protein_quinoa_text","component":"Text","text":"~4.4 grams","weight":1.5},{"id":"protein_rice_text","component":"Text","text":"~2.7 grams","weight":1.5},{"id":"fiber_row","component":"Row","children":["fiber_label_text","fiber_quinoa_text","fiber_rice_text"]},{"id":"fiber_label_text","component":"Text","text":"Fiber","weight":2},{"id":"fiber_quinoa_text","component":"Text","text":"~2.8 grams","weight":1.5},{"id":"fiber_rice_text","component":"Text","text":"~1.8 grams","weight":1.5},{"id":"gi_row","component":"Row","children":["gi_label_text","gi_quinoa_text","gi_rice_text"]},{"id":"gi_label_text","component":"Text","text":"Glycemic Index (GI)","weight":2},{"id":"gi_quinoa_text","component":"Text","text":"~53 (Moderate)","weight":1.5},{"id":"gi_rice_text","component":"Text","text":"~55 (Moderate)","weight":1.5},{"id":"gi_notes_card","component":"Card","child":"gi_notes_column"},{"id":"gi_notes_column","component":"Column","children":["gi_notes_header","gi_notes_text"]},{"id":"gi_notes_header","component":"Text","variant":"h4","text":"Glycemic Index Notes"},{"id":"gi_notes_text","component":"Text","text":"- A Glycemic Index (GI) of 55 or less is considered low.\n- A GI between 56 and 69 is considered moderate.\n- A GI of 70 or higher is considered high.\nBoth quinoa and brown rice fall within the moderate GI range, meaning they cause a relatively steady rise in blood sugar compared to high GI foods."},{"id":"actions_row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceAround","children":["quinoa_button","rice_button"]},{"id":"quinoa_button","component":"Button","child":"quinoa_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://example.com/quinoa-recipes"}}}},{"id":"quinoa_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Explore Quinoa Recipes"},{"id":"rice_button","component":"Button","child":"rice_button_text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":"https://example.com/brown-rice-recipes"}}}},{"id":"rice_button_text","component":"Text","text":"Explore Brown Rice Recipes"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: quinoa-vs-rice-comparison-1\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: quinoa-vs-rice-comparison-1\n      components[32]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[5]: assumptions_text,summary_text,comparison_card,gi_notes_card,actions_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: assumptions_text\n          text: \"Assumptions:\\n- Nutritional values are based on 100g of cooked, plain quinoa and 100g of cooked, plain long-grain brown rice, prepared with water and no added fats or seasonings.\\n- Glycemic Index (GI) values are approximate and can vary based on preparation, specific variety, and individual metabolic response.\"\n          variant: caption\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary_text\n          text: \"Summary:\\nBoth cooked quinoa and cooked brown rice are nutritious whole grains, offering good sources of protein and fiber. Quinoa generally provides a higher protein and fiber content per 100g serving compared to brown rice. Their glycemic index values are similar, both falling into the moderate category.\"\n          variant: body\n        - child: comparison_column\n          component: Card\n          id: comparison_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: comparison_column\n          children[6]: comparison_header,table_header_row,table_divider,protein_row,fiber_row,gi_row\n        - component: Text\n          id: comparison_header\n          text: Nutritional Comparison (per 100g cooked)\n          variant: h3\n        - component: Row\n          id: table_header_row\n          children[3]: nutrient_header_text,quinoa_header_text,rice_header_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: nutrient_header_text\n          text: Nutrient\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: quinoa_header_text\n          text: Cooked Quinoa (100g)\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Text\n          id: rice_header_text\n          text: Cooked Brown Rice (100g)\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Divider\n          id: table_divider\n        - component: Row\n          id: protein_row\n          children[3]: protein_label_text,protein_quinoa_text,protein_rice_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: protein_label_text\n          text: Protein\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: protein_quinoa_text\n          text: ~4.4 grams\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Text\n          id: protein_rice_text\n          text: ~2.7 grams\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Row\n          id: fiber_row\n          children[3]: fiber_label_text,fiber_quinoa_text,fiber_rice_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: fiber_label_text\n          text: Fiber\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: fiber_quinoa_text\n          text: ~2.8 grams\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Text\n          id: fiber_rice_text\n          text: ~1.8 grams\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Row\n          id: gi_row\n          children[3]: gi_label_text,gi_quinoa_text,gi_rice_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: gi_label_text\n          text: Glycemic Index (GI)\n          weight: 2\n        - component: Text\n          id: gi_quinoa_text\n          text: ~53 (Moderate)\n          weight: 1.5\n        - component: Text\n          id: gi_rice_text\n          text: ~55 (Moderate)\n          weight: 1.5\n        - child: gi_notes_column\n          component: Card\n          id: gi_notes_card\n        - component: Column\n          id: gi_notes_column\n          children[2]: gi_notes_header,gi_notes_text\n        - component: Text\n          id: gi_notes_header\n          text: Glycemic Index Notes\n          variant: h4\n        - component: Text\n          id: gi_notes_text\n          text: \"- A Glycemic Index (GI) of 55 or less is considered low.\\n- A GI between 56 and 69 is considered moderate.\\n- A GI of 70 or higher is considered high.\\nBoth quinoa and brown rice fall within the moderate GI range, meaning they cause a relatively steady rise in blood sugar compared to high GI foods.\"\n        - component: Row\n          id: actions_row\n          justify: spaceAround\n          children[2]: quinoa_button,rice_button\n        - child: quinoa_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: quinoa_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://example.com/quinoa-recipes\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: quinoa_button_text\n          text: Explore Quinoa Recipes\n        - child: rice_button_text\n          component: Button\n          id: rice_button\n          action:\n            functionCall:\n              call: openUrl\n              args:\n                url: \"https://example.com/brown-rice-recipes\"\n        - component: Text\n          id: rice_button_text\n          text: Explore Brown Rice Recipes","validation":{"json_parse_ok":true,"schema_valid_strict":true,"schema_valid_lenient":true,"toon_roundtrip_ok":true,"errors":[],"repair_attempts":0,"repair_needed":false},"metrics":{"content_coverage":0.9787234042553191,"dup_rate":0.25675675675675674,"lint_score":1.0,"output_tokens_toon":454,"output_tokens_json":438,"component_count":32.0,"unique_component_types":6.0,"max_tree_depth":5.0,"avg_tree_depth":1.625,"container_to_text_ratio":0.5263157894736842,"information_chunking_score":0.735269000853971,"ui_modularity_score":0.21875,"ui_decom