{"ui_id":"u_000681_01","response_id":"r_000681_01","query_id":"q_000681","intent":"Navigation","tags":["travel","itinerary","walking-tour"],"intent_bucket":"navigation","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"rome-walking-tour-surface","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateDataModel":{"surfaceId":"rome-walking-tour-surface","path":"/","value":{"title":"Rome Historic Center Walking Tour: 2025-05-15","summary":"This walking tour provides a detailed itinerary for exploring Rome's historic center on May 15, 2025, starting at the Colosseum and concluding at Piazza Navona. The route includes the Roman Forum, Palatine Hill, and the Pantheon, with estimated walking times and a designated lunch break.","itinerary":[{"time":"09:00 - 10:30","activity":"Visit the Colosseum","duration":"1 hour 30 min","notes":"Start your day exploring this iconic amphitheater. Pre-booking tickets is highly recommended.","icon":"/icons/landmark.png","image":"/images/colosseum_rome.jpg"},{"time":"10:30 - 10:45","activity":"Walk to Roman Forum / Palatine Hill","duration":"15 min","notes":"Exit the Colosseum and walk to the main entrance for the Roman Forum and Palatine Hill, which is typically across Via dei Fori Imperiali or via the Palatine Hill entrance.","icon":"/icons/walking.png"},{"time":"10:45 - 13:00","activity":"Explore the Roman Forum & Palatine Hill","duration":"2 hours 15 min","notes":"Wander through the ruins of ancient Rome. The Palatine Hill offers great views over the Forum and Circus Maximus.","icon":"/icons/landmark.png","image":"/images/roman_forum_rome.jpg"},{"time":"13:00 - 13:30","activity":"Walk to Pantheon area","duration":"30 min","notes":"Exit the Roman Forum (e.g., near Capitoline Hill/Piazza Venezia) and walk towards the Pantheon. This walk takes you through bustling Roman streets.","icon":"/icons/walking.png"},{"time":"13:30 - 14:30","activity":"Lunch Break","duration":"1 hour","notes":"Enjoy lunch at one of the many trattorias or cafes in the charming streets surrounding the Pantheon.","icon":"/icons/restaurant.png"},{"time":"14:30 - 15:15","activity":"Visit the Pantheon","duration":"45 min","notes":"Marvel at the architectural wonder of the Pantheon, a former Roman temple, now a church. Entry is typically free, but be prepared for queues.","icon":"/icons/landmark.png","image":"/images/pantheon_rome.jpg"},{"time":"15:15 - 15:25","activity":"Walk to Piazza Navona","duration":"10 min","notes":"A short stroll from the Pantheon will lead you directly to Piazza Navona.","icon":"/icons/walking.png"},{"time":"15:25 - 17:00","activity":"Explore Piazza Navona","duration":"1 hour 35 min","notes":"Enjoy the beautiful fountains (Bernini's Fountain of Four Rivers), street artists, and vibrant atmosphere of Piazza Navona. You'll have ample time to soak it all in before 17:00.","icon":"/icons/landmark.png","image":"/images/piazza_navona_rome.jpg"}],"assumptions":["An average walking pace of 4 km/h (2.5 mph) is used for time estimates.","The Roman Forum and Palatine Hill are treated as one combined visit, as they share an entrance ticket.","The Colosseum visit assumes you have pre-booked tickets to optimize entry time.","The lunch break is planned immediately after visiting the Roman Forum/Palatine Hill and before the Pantheon.","Visiting times for each attraction are estimates and can vary based on personal interest and crowd levels."],"tips":["Wear comfortable walking shoes. Rome's historic center has many cobblestone streets.","Stay hydrated. Carry a water bottle; there are public drinking fountains (nasoni) throughout the city.","Book tickets for the Colosseum and Roman Forum/Palatine Hill in advance to save time and ensure entry.","Be aware of your surroundings and keep an eye on your belongings in crowded areas.","Consider downloading an offline map of Rome."],"quickActions":[{"label":"Book Colosseum Tickets","url":"https://www.coopculture.it/en/"},{"label":"Find Restaurants near Pantheon","url":"https://www.example.com/rome/restaurants-near-pantheon"},{"label":"Explore Rome Walking Tours","url":"https://www.example.com/rome/walking-tours"}],"icons":{"itinerary":"/icons/travel_itinerary.png"}}}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"rome-walking-tour-surface","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["header-row","summary-text","main-tabs","actions-divider","actions-header","actions-row"]},{"id":"header-row","component":"Row","align":"center","children":["header-icon","header-title"]},{"id":"header-icon","component":"Image","variant":"icon","url":{"path":"/icons/itinerary"}},{"id":"header-title","component":"Text","variant":"h2","text":{"path":"/title"}},{"id":"summary-text","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":{"path":"/summary"}},{"id":"main-tabs","component":"Tabs","tabs":[{"title":"Itinerary","child":"itinerary-list"},{"title":"Assumptions & Tips","child":"info-column"}]},{"id":"itinerary-list","component":"List","direction":"vertical","children":{"componentId":"itinerary-item-template","path":"/itinerary"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-template","component":"Card","child":"itinerary-item-content"},{"id":"itinerary-item-content","component":"Column","children":["itinerary-item-image","itinerary-item-details-row","itinerary-item-notes"]},{"id":"itinerary-item-image","component":"Image","variant":"smallFeature","url":{"path":"image"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-details-row","component":"Row","align":"center","children":["itinerary-item-icon","itinerary-item-text-col"]},{"id":"itinerary-item-icon","component":"Image","variant":"icon","url":{"path":"icon"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-text-col","component":"Column","children":["itinerary-item-activity","itinerary-item-time","itinerary-item-duration"]},{"id":"itinerary-item-activity","component":"Text","variant":"h5","text":{"path":"activity"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-time","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":{"path":"time"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-duration","component":"Text","variant":"caption","text":{"path":"duration"}},{"id":"itinerary-item-notes","component":"Text","variant":"body","text":{"path":"notes"}},{"id":"info-column","component":"Column","children":["assumptions-header","assumptions-list","info-divider","tips-header","tips-list"]},{"id":"assumptions-header","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Assumptions"},{"id":"assumptions-list","component":"List","direction":"vertical","children":{"componentId":"list-item-template","path":"/assumptions"}},{"id":"info-divider","component":"Divider"},{"id":"tips-header","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Tips for Your Tour"},{"id":"tips-list","component":"List","direction":"vertical","children":{"componentId":"list-item-template","path":"/tips"}},{"id":"list-item-template","component":"Text","text":{"path":""}},{"id":"actions-divider","component":"Divider"},{"id":"actions-header","component":"Text","variant":"h3","text":"Quick Actions"},{"id":"actions-row","component":"Row","justify":"spaceAround","children":{"componentId":"quick-action-button-template","path":"/quickActions"}},{"id":"quick-action-button-template","component":"Button","child":"quick-action-button-text","action":{"functionCall":{"call":"openUrl","args":{"url":{"path":"url"}},"returnType":"void"}}},{"id":"quick-action-button-text","component":"Text","text":{"path":"label"}}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[3]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: rome-walking-tour-surface\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateDataModel:\n      path: /\n      surfaceId: rome-walking-tour-surface\n      value:\n        summary: \"This walking tour provides a detailed itinerary for exploring Rome's historic center on May 15, 2025, starting at the Colosseum and concluding at Piazza Navona. The route includes the Roman Forum, Palatine Hill, and the Pantheon, with estimated walking times and a designated lunch break.\"\n        title: \"Rome Historic Center Walking Tour: 2025-05-15\"\n        assumptions[5]: An average walking pace of 4 km/h (2.5 mph) is used for time estimates.,\"The Roman Forum and Palatine Hill are treated as one combined visit, as they share an entrance ticket.\",The Colosseum visit assumes you have pre-booked tickets to optimize entry time.,The lunch break is planned immediately after visiting the Roman Forum/Palatine Hill and before the Pantheon.,Visiting times for each attraction are estimates and can vary based on personal interest and crowd levels.\n        icons:\n          itinerary: /icons/travel_itinerary.png\n        itinerary[8]:\n          - activity: Visit the Colosseum\n            duration: 1 hour 30 min\n            icon: /icons/landmark.png\n            image: /images/colosseum_rome.jpg\n            notes: Start your day exploring this iconic amphitheater. Pre-booking tickets is highly recommended.\n            time: \"09:00 - 10:30\"\n          - activity: Walk to Roman Forum / Palatine Hill\n            duration: 15 min\n            icon: /icons/walking.png\n            notes: \"Exit the Colosseum and walk to the main entrance for the Roman Forum and Palatine Hill, which is typically across Via dei Fori Imperiali or via the Palatine Hill entrance.\"\n            time: \"10:30 - 10:45\"\n          - activity: Explore the Roman Forum & Palatine Hill\n            duration: 2 hours 15 min\n            icon: /icons/landmark.png\n            image: /images/roman_forum_rome.jpg\n            notes: Wander through the ruins of ancient Rome. The Palatine Hill offers great views over the Forum and Circus Maximus.\n            time: \"10:45 - 13:00\"\n          - activity: Walk to Pantheon area\n            duration: 30 min\n            icon: /icons/walking.png\n            notes: \"Exit the Roman Forum (e.g., near Capitoline Hill/Piazza Venezia) and walk towards the Pantheon. This walk takes you through bustling Roman streets.\"\n            time: \"13:00 - 13:30\"\n          - activity: Lunch Break\n            duration: 1 hour\n            icon: /icons/restaurant.png\n            notes: Enjoy lunch at one of the many trattorias or cafes in the charming streets surrounding the Pantheon.\n            time: \"13:30 - 14:30\"\n          - activity: Visit the Pantheon\n            duration: 45 min\n            icon: /icons/landmark.png\n            image: /images/pantheon_rome.jpg\n            notes: \"Marvel at the architectural wonder of the Pantheon, a former Roman temple, now a church. Entry is typically free, but be prepared for queues.\"\n            time: \"14:30 - 15:15\"\n          - activity: Walk to Piazza Navona\n            duration: 10 min\n            icon: /icons/walking.png\n            notes: A short stroll from the Pantheon will lead you directly to Piazza Navona.\n            time: \"15:15 - 15:25\"\n          - activity: Explore Piazza Navona\n            duration: 1 hour 35 min\n            icon: /icons/landmark.png\n            image: /images/piazza_navona_rome.jpg\n            notes: \"Enjoy the beautiful fountains (Bernini's Fountain of Four Rivers), street artists, and vibrant atmosphere of Piazza Navona. You'll have ample time to soak it all in before 17:00.\"\n            time: \"15:25 - 17:00\"\n        quickActions[3]{label,url}:\n          Book Colosseum Tickets,\"https://www.coopculture.it/en/\"\n          Find Restaurants near Pantheon,\"https://www.example.com/rome/restaurants-near-pantheon\"\n          Explore Rome Walking Tours,\"https://www.example.com/rome/walking-tours\"\n        tips[5]: Wear comfortable walking shoes. Rome's historic center has many cobblestone streets.,Stay hydrated. Carry a water bottle; there are public drinking fountains (nasoni) throughout the city.,Book tickets for the Colosseum and Roman Forum/Palatine Hill in advance to save time and ensure entry.,Be aware of your surroundings and keep an eye on your belongings in crowded areas.,Consider downloading an offline map of Rome.\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: rome-walking-tour-surface\n      components[29]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[6]: header-row,summary-text,main-tabs,actions-divider,actions-header,actions-row\n        - align: center\n          component: Row\n          id: header-row\n          children[2]: header-icon,header-title\n        - component: Image\n          id: header-icon\n          variant: icon\n          url:\n            path: /icons/itinerary\n        - component: Text\n          id: header-title\n          variant: h2\n          text:\n            path: /title\n        - component: Text\n          id: summary-text\n          variant: body\n          text:\n            path: /summary\n        - component: Tabs\n          id: main-tabs\n          tabs[2]{child,title}:\n            itinerary-list,Itinerary\n            info-column,Assumptions & Tips\n        - component: List\n          direction: vertical\n          id: itinerary-list\n          children:\n            componentId: itinerary-item-template\n            path: /itinerary\n        - child: itinerary-item-content\n          component: Card\n          id: itinerary-item-template\n        - component: Column\n          id: itinerary-item-content\n          children[3]: itinerary-item-image,itinerary-item-details-row,itinerary-item-notes\n        - component: Image\n          id: itinerary-item-image\n          variant: smallFeature\n          url:\n            path: image\n        - align: center\n          component: Row\n          id: itinerary-item-details-row\n          children[2]: itinerary-item-icon,itinerary-item-text-col\n        - component: Image\n          id: itinerary-item-icon\n          variant: icon\n          url:\n            path: icon\n        - component: Column\n          id: itinerary-item-text-col\n          children[3]: itinerary-item-activity,itinerary-item-time,itinerary-item-duration